":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3358":{"id":"/changelog-327","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-3","content":"Revset expressions like hidden_id | description(x) now search the specified\nhidden revision and its ancestors as well\nas all visible revisions."},"3359":{"id":"/changelog-328","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-3","content":"Commit templates no longer normalize description by appending final newline\ncharacter. Use description.trim_end() ++ \"\\n\" if needed."},"3360":{"id":"/changelog-329","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-3","content":"The git.push-bookmark-prefix setting is deprecated in favor of\ntemplates.git_push_bookmark, which supports templating. The old setting can\nbe expressed in template as \"<prefix>\" ++ change_id.short()."},"3361":{"id":"/changelog-330","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"New change_id(prefix)/commit_id(prefix) revset functions to explicitly\nquery commits by change/commit ID prefix."},"3362":{"id":"/changelog-331","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"The parents() and children() revset functions now accept an optional\ndepth argument. For instance, parents(x, 3) is equivalent to x---, and\nchildren(x, 3) is equivalent to x+++."},"3363":{"id":"/changelog-332","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"jj evolog can now follow changes from multiple revisions such as divergent\nrevisions."},"3364":{"id":"/changelog-333","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"jj diff now accepts -T/--template option to customize summary output."},"3365":{"id":"/changelog-334","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"Log node templates are now specified in toml rather than hardcoded."},"3366":{"id":"/changelog-335","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"Templates now support json(x) function to serialize values in JSON format."},"3367":{"id":"/changelog-336","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-3","content":"The ANSI 256-color palette can be used when configuring colors. For example,\ncolors.\"diff removed token\" = { bg = \"ansi-color-52\", underline = false }\nwill apply a dark red background on removed words in diffs."},"3368":{"id":"/changelog-337","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-3","content":"jj file annotate can now process files at a hidden revision."},"3369":{"id":"/changelog-338","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-3","content":"jj op log --op-diff no longer fails at displaying \"reconcile divergent\noperations.\" #4465"},"3370":{"id":"/changelog-339","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-3","content":"jj util gc --expire=now now passes the corresponding flag to git gc."},"3371":{"id":"/changelog-340","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-3","content":"change_id/commit_id.shortest() template functions now take conflicting\nbookmark and tag names into account.\n#2416"},"3372":{"id":"/changelog-341","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-3","content":"Fixed lockfile issue on stale file handles observed with NFS."},"3373":{"id":"/changelog-342","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#packaging-changes-1","content":"aarch64-windows builds (release binaries and main snapshots) are now provided."},"3374":{"id":"/changelog-343","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3375":{"id":"/changelog-344","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Anton Älgmyr (@algmyr)"},"3376":{"id":"/changelog-345","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3377":{"id":"/changelog-346","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Benjamin Brittain (@benbrittain)"},"3378":{"id":"/changelog-347","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Cyril Plisko (@imp)"},"3379":{"id":"/changelog-348","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Daniel Luz (@mernen)"},"3380":{"id":"/changelog-349","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Gaëtan Lehmann (@glehmann)"},"3381":{"id":"/changelog-350","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Gilad Woloch (@giladwo)"},"3382":{"id":"/changelog-351","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Greg Morenz (@gmorenz)"},"3383":{"id":"/changelog-352","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Igor Velkov (@iav)"},"3384":{"id":"/changelog-353","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3385":{"id":"/changelog-354","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Jade Lovelace (@lf-)"},"3386":{"id":"/changelog-355","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Jonas Greitemann (@jgreitemann)"},"3387":{"id":"/changelog-356","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Josh Steadmon (@steadmon)"},"3388":{"id":"/changelog-357","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"juemrami (@juemrami)"},"3389":{"id":"/changelog-358","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Kaiyi Li (@06393993)"},"3390":{"id":"/changelog-359","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Lars Francke (@lfrancke)"},"3391":{"id":"/changelog-360","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3392":{"id":"/changelog-361","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Osama Qarem (@osamaqarem)"},"3393":{"id":"/changelog-362","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3394":{"id":"/changelog-363","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"raylu (@raylu)"},"3395":{"id":"/changelog-364","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3396":{"id":"/changelog-365","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3397":{"id":"/changelog-366","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-2","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3398":{"id":"/changelog-367","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-1","content":"The experimental support from release 0.29.0 for transferring the change ID\nto/from Git remotes has been enabled by default. The change ID is stored in\nthe Git commit itself (in a commit header called change-id), which means\nit will be transferred by regular git push etc. Please let us know if you\nrun into any problems with it. You can disable it setting\ngit.write-change-id-header. Note that some Git remotes (e.g GitLab) and\nsome Git commands (e.g. git rebase) do not preserve the change ids when\nthey rewrite commits."},"3399":{"id":"/changelog-368","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-1","content":"jj rebase now automatically abandons divergent commits if another commit\nwith the same change ID is already present in the destination with identical\nchanges."},"3400":{"id":"/changelog-369","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-1","content":"jj split has gained --message, --insert-before, --insert-after, and\n--destination options."},"3401":{"id":"/changelog-370","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-1","content":"jj evolog can show associated operations for commits created by new jj\nversions."},"3402":{"id":"/changelog-371","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"The old libgit2 code path for fetches and pushes has been removed,\nand the git.subprocess setting along with it."},"3403":{"id":"/changelog-372","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"In templates, bookmark/tag/remote names are now formatted in revset symbol\nnotation. The type of bookmark.remote() is changed to Option<_>.\nbookmark.remote() == \"foo\" still works, but bookmark.remote().<method>()\nmight need if(bookmark.remote(), ..) to suppress error."},"3404":{"id":"/changelog-373","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"jj rebase now automatically abandons divergent commits if another commit\nwith the same change ID is already present in the destination with identical\nchanges. To keep these divergent commits, use the --keep-divergent flag."},"3405":{"id":"/changelog-374","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"The deprecated --skip-empty flag for jj rebase has been removed. Use the\n--skip-emptied flag instead."},"3406":{"id":"/changelog-375","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"The deprecated jj branch subcommands have been removed. Use the jj\nbookmark subcommands instead."},"3407":{"id":"/changelog-376","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"jj util completion now requires the name of the shell as a positional\nargument and no longer produces Bash completions by default. The deprecated\noptional arguments for different shells have been removed."},"3408":{"id":"/changelog-377","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"External diff tools are now run in the temporary directory containing\nthe before (left) and after (right) directories, making diffs appear\nmore pleasing for tools that display file paths prominently. Users can\nopt out of this by setting merge-tools.<tool>.diff-do-chdir = false,\nbut this will likely be removed in a future release. Please report any\nissues you run into."},"3409":{"id":"/changelog-378","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-4","content":"The minimum supported Rust version (MSRV) is now 1.85.0."},"3410":{"id":"/changelog-379","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-4","content":"The ui.diff.format and ui.diff.tool config options have been merged as\nui.diff-formatter. The builtin format can be specified as :<format>\n(e.g. ui.diff-formatter=\":git\" for Git diffs.)"},"3411":{"id":"/changelog-380","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-4","content":"The .normal_hex() method will be removed from the CommitId template type.\nIt's useful only for the ChangeId type."},"3412":{"id":"/changelog-381","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-4","content":"jj split has gained a --message option to set the description of the\ncommit with the selected changes."},"3413":{"id":"/changelog-382","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-4","content":"jj split has gained the ability to place the revision with the selected\nchanges anywhere in the revision tree with the --insert-before,\n--insert-after and --destination command line flags."},"3414":{"id":"/changelog-383","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-4","content":"Added git.track-default-bookmark-on-clone setting to control whether to\ntrack the default remote bookmark on jj git clone."},"3415":{"id":"/changelog-384","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-4","content":"Templates can now do arithmetic on integers with the +, -, *, /, and\n% infix operators."},"3416":{"id":"/changelog-385","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-4","content":"Evolution history is now stored in the operation log. jj evolog can show\nassociated operations for commits created by new jj versions."},"3417":{"id":"/changelog-386","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-4","content":"Work around a git issue that could cause subprocess operations to hang if the\ncore.fsmonitor gitconfig is set in the global or system gitconfigs.\n#6440"},"3418":{"id":"/changelog-387","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-4","content":"jj parallelize can now parallelize groups of changes that start with an\nimmutable change, but do not contain any other immutable changes."},"3419":{"id":"/changelog-388","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-4","content":"jj will no longer warn about deprecated paths on macOS if the configured\nXDG directory is the deprecated one (~/Library/Application Support)."},"3420":{"id":"/changelog-389","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-4","content":"The builtin diff editor now correctly handles splitting changes where a file\nis replaced by a directory of the same name.\n#5189"},"3421":{"id":"/changelog-390","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#packaging-changes-2","content":"Due to the removal of the libgit2 code path, packagers should remove any\ndependencies on libgit2, libssh2, Zlib, OpenSSL, and pkg-config, and\nensure they are not setting the Cargo git2 or vendored-openssl features."},"3422":{"id":"/changelog-391","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3423":{"id":"/changelog-392","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Alper Cugun (@alper)"},"3424":{"id":"/changelog-393","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3425":{"id":"/changelog-394","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Benjamin Brittain (@benbrittain)"},"3426":{"id":"/changelog-395","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3427":{"id":"/changelog-396","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Bryce Berger (@bryceberger)"},"3428":{"id":"/changelog-397","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Colin Nelson (@orthros)"},"3429":{"id":"/changelog-398","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Doug Stephen (@dljsjr)"},"3430":{"id":"/changelog-399","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Emily (@emilazy)"},"3431":{"id":"/changelog-400","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Eyvind Bernhardsen (@eyvind)"},"3432":{"id":"/changelog-401","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Felix Geisendörfer (@felixge)"},"3433":{"id":"/changelog-402","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Gaëtan Lehmann (@glehmann)"},"3434":{"id":"/changelog-403","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3435":{"id":"/changelog-404","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Isaac Corbrey (@icorbrey)"},"3436":{"id":"/changelog-405","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Jonas Greitemann (@jgreitemann)"},"3437":{"id":"/changelog-406","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Josep Mengual (@truita)"},"3438":{"id":"/changelog-407","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"kkoang (@kkoang)"},"3439":{"id":"/changelog-408","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Manuel Mendez (@mmlb)"},"3440":{"id":"/changelog-409","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Marshall Bowers (@maxdeviant)"},"3441":{"id":"/changelog-410","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3442":{"id":"/changelog-411","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Mateus Auler (@mateusauler)"},"3443":{"id":"/changelog-412","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Michael Pratt (@prattmic)"},"3444":{"id":"/changelog-413","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Nicole Patricia Mazzuca (@strega-nil)"},"3445":{"id":"/changelog-414","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3446":{"id":"/changelog-415","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3447":{"id":"/changelog-416","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"T6 (@tjjfvi)"},"3448":{"id":"/changelog-417","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3449":{"id":"/changelog-418","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Winter (@winterqt)"},"3450":{"id":"/changelog-419","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-3","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3451":{"id":"/changelog-420","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-2","content":"Experimental support for transferring the change ID to/from Git remotes behind configuration\nsetting git.write-change-id-header. If this is enabled, the change ID will be stored in the Git\ncommit itself (in a commit header called change-id), which means it will be transferred by\nregular git push etc. This is an evolving feature that currently defaults to \"false\". This\ndefault will likely change in the future as we gain confidence with forge support and user\nexpectations."},"3452":{"id":"/changelog-421","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-5","content":"jj git push -c/--change no longer moves existing local bookmarks."},"3453":{"id":"/changelog-422","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-5","content":"The editor-*.jjdescription files passed to your editor by e.g. jj describe\nare now written to your system's temporary directory instead of .jj/repo/."},"3454":{"id":"/changelog-423","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-5","content":"git.subprocess = false has been deprecated, and the old libgit2\ncode path for fetches and pushes will be removed entirely in 0.30.\nPlease report any remaining issues you have with the Git\nsubprocessing path."},"3455":{"id":"/changelog-424","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-5","content":"ui.default-description has been deprecated, and will be migrated to\ntemplate-aliases.default_commit_description. Please also consider using\ntemplates.draft_commit_description,\nand/or templates.commit_trailers."},"3456":{"id":"/changelog-425","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-5","content":"On macOS, config.toml files in ~/Library/Application Support/jj are\ndeprecated; one should instead use $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jj\n(defaults to ~/.config/jj)"},"3457":{"id":"/changelog-426","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"Color-words diff has gained an option to compare conflict pairs without\nmaterializing."},"3458":{"id":"/changelog-427","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"jj show patches can now be suppressed with --no-patch."},"3459":{"id":"/changelog-428","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"Added ui.bookmark-list-sort-keys setting to configure default sort keys for the\njj bookmark list command."},"3460":{"id":"/changelog-429","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"New signed revset function to filter for cryptographically signed commits."},"3461":{"id":"/changelog-430","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"jj describe, jj commit, jj new, jj squash and jj split add the\ncommit trailers, configured in the commit_trailers template, to the commit\ndescription. Use cases include DCO Sign Off and Gerrit Change Id."},"3462":{"id":"/changelog-431","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"Added duplicate_description template, which allows customizing the descriptions\nof the commits jj duplicate creates."},"3463":{"id":"/changelog-432","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"jj absorb can now squash a deleted file if it was added by one of the\ndestination revisions."},"3464":{"id":"/changelog-433","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"Added ui.streampager.show-ruler setting to configure whether the ruler should be\nshown when the builtin pager starts up."},"3465":{"id":"/changelog-434","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"jj git fetch now warns instead of erroring for unknown git.fetch remotes\nif other remotes are available."},"3466":{"id":"/changelog-435","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"Commit objects in templates now have trailers() -> List<Trailer>, the Trailer\nobjects have key() -> String and value() -> String."},"3467":{"id":"/changelog-436","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"jj config edit will now roll back to previous version if a syntax error has been introduced in the new config."},"3468":{"id":"/changelog-437","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-5","content":"When using dynamic command-line completion, revision names will be completed\nin more complex expressions. For example, typing\njj log -r first-bookmark..sec and then pressing Tab could complete the\nexpression to first-bookmark..second-bookmark."},"3469":{"id":"/changelog-438","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-5","content":"Fixed crash on change-delete conflict resolution.\n#6250"},"3470":{"id":"/changelog-439","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-5","content":"The builtin diff editor now tries to preserve unresolved conflicts.\n#4963"},"3471":{"id":"/changelog-440","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-5","content":"Fixed bash and zsh shell completion when completing aliases of multiple arguments.\n#5377"},"3472":{"id":"/changelog-441","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#packaging-changes-3","content":"Jujutsu now uses\nzlib-rs, a\nfast compression library written in Rust. Packagers should remove any\ndependency on CMake and drop the packaging Cargo feature."},"3473":{"id":"/changelog-442","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3474":{"id":"/changelog-443","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Aleksey Kuznetsov (@zummenix)"},"3475":{"id":"/changelog-444","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3476":{"id":"/changelog-445","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Benjamin Brittain (@benbrittain)"},"3477":{"id":"/changelog-446","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3478":{"id":"/changelog-447","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Caleb White (@calebdw)"},"3479":{"id":"/changelog-448","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Daniel Luz (@mernen)"},"3480":{"id":"/changelog-449","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-4","content":"Emily (@emilazy)"},"3481":{"id":"/changelog-450","page_id":"/changelog","ta