changelog#contributors-6","content":"Jonathan Gilchrist (@jgilchrist)"},"3577":{"id":"/changelog-546","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Kenyon Ralph (@kenyon)"},"3578":{"id":"/changelog-547","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Lucas Garron (@lgarron)"},"3579":{"id":"/changelog-548","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3580":{"id":"/changelog-549","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Nick Pupko (@npupko)"},"3581":{"id":"/changelog-550","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3582":{"id":"/changelog-551","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Raphael Borun Das Gupta (@das-g)"},"3583":{"id":"/changelog-552","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Remo Senekowitsch (@senekor)"},"3584":{"id":"/changelog-553","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Robin Stocker (@robinst)"},"3585":{"id":"/changelog-554","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3586":{"id":"/changelog-555","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Siva Mahadevan (@svmhdvn)"},"3587":{"id":"/changelog-556","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3588":{"id":"/changelog-557","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-6","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3589":{"id":"/changelog-558","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-4","content":"git.subprocess is now enabled by default, improving compatibility with Git\nfetches and pushes by spawning an external git process. Users can opt out\nof this by setting git.subprocess = false, but this will likely be removed\nin a future release. Please report any issues you run into."},"3590":{"id":"/changelog-559","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"Bookmark name to be created/updated is now parsed as a revset\nsymbol. Quotation may be needed in addition to shell\nquotes. Example: jj bookmark create -r@- \"'name with space'\""},"3591":{"id":"/changelog-560","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"jj bookmark create, jj bookmark set and jj bookmark move onto a hidden\ncommit make it visible."},"3592":{"id":"/changelog-561","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"jj bookmark forget now untracks any corresponding remote bookmarks instead\nof forgetting them, since forgetting a remote bookmark can be unintuitive.\nThe old behavior is still available with the new --include-remotes flag."},"3593":{"id":"/changelog-562","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"jj fix now always sets the working directory of invoked tools to be the\nworkspace root, instead of the working directory of the jj fix."},"3594":{"id":"/changelog-563","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"The ui.allow-filesets configuration option has been removed.\nThe \"fileset\" language has been enabled by default since v0.20."},"3595":{"id":"/changelog-564","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-7","content":"templates.annotate_commit_summary is renamed to templates.file_annotate,\nand now has an implicit self parameter of type AnnotationLine, instead of\nCommit. All methods on Commit can be accessed with commit.method(), or\nself.commit().method()."},"3596":{"id":"/changelog-565","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-7","content":"This release takes the first steps to make target revision required in\nbookmark create, bookmark move and bookmark set. Those commands will display\na warning if the user does not specify target revision explicitly. In the near\nfuture those commands will fail if target revision is not specified."},"3597":{"id":"/changelog-566","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-7","content":"The signing.sign-all config option has been deprecated in favor of\nsigning.behavior. The new option accepts drop (never sign), keep (preserve\nexisting signatures), own (sign own commits), or force (sign all commits).\nExisting signing.sign-all = true translates to signing.behavior = \"own\", and\nfalse translates to \"keep\". Invalid configuration is now an error."},"3598":{"id":"/changelog-567","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"The new jj sign and jj unsign commands allow for signing/unsigning commits.\njj sign supports configuring the default revset through revsets.sign when\nno --revisions arguments are provided."},"3599":{"id":"/changelog-568","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"jj git fetch now supports string pattern syntax\non --remote option and git.fetch configuration."},"3600":{"id":"/changelog-569","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Template functions truncate_start() and truncate_end() gained an optional\nellipsis parameter; passing this prepends or appends the ellipsis to the\ncontent if it is truncated to fit the maximum width."},"3601":{"id":"/changelog-570","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Templates now support stringify(x) function and string method\n.escape_json(). The latter serializes the string in JSON format. It is\nuseful for making machine-readable templates by escaping problematic\ncharacters like \\n."},"3602":{"id":"/changelog-571","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Templates now support trim(), trim_start() and trim_end() methods\nwhich remove whitespace from the start and end of a String type."},"3603":{"id":"/changelog-572","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"The description of commits backed out by jj backout can now be configured\nusing templates.backout_description."},"3604":{"id":"/changelog-573","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"New AnnotationLine templater type. Used in templates.file_annotate.\nProvides self.commit(), .content(), .line_number(), and\n.first_line_in_hunk()."},"3605":{"id":"/changelog-574","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Templates now have format_short_operation_id(id) function for users to\ncustomize the default operation id representation."},"3606":{"id":"/changelog-575","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"The jj init/jj revert stubs that print errors can now be overridden with\naliases. All of jj clone/init/revert add a hint to a generic error."},"3607":{"id":"/changelog-576","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Help text is now colored (when stdout is a terminal)."},"3608":{"id":"/changelog-577","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"Commands that used to suggest --ignore-immutable now print the number of\nimmutable commits that would be rewritten if used and a link to the docs."},"3609":{"id":"/changelog-578","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-7","content":"jj undo now shows a hint when undoing an undo operation that the user may\nbe looking for jj op restore instead."},"3610":{"id":"/changelog-579","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-9","content":"jj status now shows untracked files under untracked directories.\n#5389"},"3611":{"id":"/changelog-580","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-9","content":"Added workaround for the bug that untracked files are ignored when watchman is\nenabled. #5728"},"3612":{"id":"/changelog-581","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-9","content":"The signing.backends.ssh.allowed-signers configuration option will now\nexpand ~/ to $HOME/.\n#5626"},"3613":{"id":"/changelog-582","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-9","content":"config-schema.json now allows arrays of strings for the settings ui.editor\nand ui.diff.tool."},"3614":{"id":"/changelog-583","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-9","content":"config-schema.json now allows an array of strings or nested table for the\nui.pager setting."},"3615":{"id":"/changelog-584","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3616":{"id":"/changelog-585","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Alain Leufroy (@aleufroy)"},"3617":{"id":"/changelog-586","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Aleksey Kuznetsov (@zummenix)"},"3618":{"id":"/changelog-587","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Alexander Mikhailov (@AM5800)"},"3619":{"id":"/changelog-588","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Andrew Gilbert (@andyg0808)"},"3620":{"id":"/changelog-589","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Antoine Martin (@alarsyo)"},"3621":{"id":"/changelog-590","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Anton Bulakh (@necauqua)"},"3622":{"id":"/changelog-591","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3623":{"id":"/changelog-592","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Baltasar Dinis (@bsdinis)"},"3624":{"id":"/changelog-593","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3625":{"id":"/changelog-594","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Bryce Berger (@bryceberger)"},"3626":{"id":"/changelog-595","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Burak Varlı (@unexge)"},"3627":{"id":"/changelog-596","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"David Rieber (@drieber)"},"3628":{"id":"/changelog-597","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Emily (@emilazy)"},"3629":{"id":"/changelog-598","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Evan Mesterhazy (@emesterhazy)"},"3630":{"id":"/changelog-599","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"George Christou (@gechr)"},"3631":{"id":"/changelog-600","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"HKalbasi (@HKalbasi)"},"3632":{"id":"/changelog-601","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3633":{"id":"/changelog-602","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Jacob Hayes (@JacobHayes)"},"3634":{"id":"/changelog-603","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Jonathan Frere (@MrJohz)"},"3635":{"id":"/changelog-604","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Jonathan Tan (@jonathantanmy)"},"3636":{"id":"/changelog-605","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Josh Steadmon (@steadmon)"},"3637":{"id":"/changelog-606","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"maan2003 (@maan2003)"},"3638":{"id":"/changelog-607","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3639":{"id":"/changelog-608","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Matthew Davidson (@KingMob)"},"3640":{"id":"/changelog-609","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3641":{"id":"/changelog-610","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Philipp Albrecht (@pylbrecht)"},"3642":{"id":"/changelog-611","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Roman Timushev (@rtimush)"},"3643":{"id":"/changelog-612","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Samuel Tardieu (@samueltardieu)"},"3644":{"id":"/changelog-613","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3645":{"id":"/changelog-614","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Stephan Hügel (@urschrei)"},"3646":{"id":"/changelog-615","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3647":{"id":"/changelog-616","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-7","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3648":{"id":"/changelog-617","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-5","content":"Improved Git push/fetch compatibility by spawning an external git process.\nThis can be enabled by the git.subprocess=true config knob, and will be the\ndefault in a future release."},"3649":{"id":"/changelog-618","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-5","content":"jj log can now show cryptographic commit signatures. The output can be\ncontrolled by the ui.show-cryptographic-signatures=true config knob."},"3650":{"id":"/changelog-619","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj abandon now deletes bookmarks pointing to the revisions to be abandoned.\nUse --retain-bookmarks to move bookmarks backwards. If deleted bookmarks\nwere tracking remote bookmarks, the associated bookmarks (or branches) will be\ndeleted from the remote on jj git push --all.\n#3505"},"3651":{"id":"/changelog-620","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj init --git and jj init --git-repo have been removed. They were\ndeprecated in early 2024. Use jj git init instead."},"3652":{"id":"/changelog-621","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The following deprecated commands have been removed:"},"3653":{"id":"/changelog-622","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj cat is replaced by jj file show."},"3654":{"id":"/changelog-623","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj chmod is replaced by jj file chmod."},"3655":{"id":"/changelog-624","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj files is replaced by jj file list."},"3656":{"id":"/changelog-625","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The deprecated -l short alias for --limit in jj log, jj op log\nand jj obslog has been removed. The -n short alias can be used instead."},"3657":{"id":"/changelog-626","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The deprecated --siblings options for jj split has been removed.\njj split --parallel can be used instead."},"3658":{"id":"/changelog-627","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The deprecated fix.tool-command config option has been removed."},"3659":{"id":"/changelog-628","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"In colocated repos, the Git index now contains the changes from all parents\nof the working copy instead of just the first parent (HEAD). 2-sided\nconflicts from the merged parents are now added to the Git index as conflicts\nas well."},"3660":{"id":"/changelog-629","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The following change introduced in 0.25.0 is reverted:"},"3661":{"id":"/changelog-630","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj config list now prints inline tables { key = value, .. } literally.\nInner items of inline tables are no longer merged across configuration\nfiles."},"3662":{"id":"/changelog-631","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj resolve will now attempt to resolve all conflicted files instead of\nresolving the first conflicted file. To resolve a single file, pass a file\npath to jj resolve."},"3663":{"id":"/changelog-632","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj util mangen is replaced with jj util install-man-pages, which can\ninstall man pages for all jj subcommands to a given path."},"3664":{"id":"/changelog-633","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"In jj config list template, value is now typed as ConfigValue, not as\nString serialized in TOML syntax."},"3665":{"id":"/changelog-634","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj git remote add/set-url now converts relative Git remote path to\nabsolute path."},"3666":{"id":"/changelog-635","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"jj log/op log now applies -n/--limit before the items are reversed.\nRationale: It's more useful to see the N most recent commits/operations, and\nis more performant. The old behavior can be achieved by jj log .. | head.\n#5403"},"3667":{"id":"/changelog-636","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"Upgraded scm-record from v0.4.0 to v0.5.0. See release notes at\nhttps://github.com/arxanas/scm-record/releases/tag/v0.5.0."},"3668":{"id":"/changelog-637","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"The builtin pager is switched to\nstreampager. It can handle large\ninputs better and can be configured."},"3669":{"id":"/changelog-638","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-8","content":"Conflicts materialized in the working copy before jj 0.19.0 may no longer\nbe parsed correctly. If you are using version 0.18.0 or earlier, check out a\nnon-conflicted commit before upgrading to prevent issues."},"3670":{"id":"/changelog-639","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj git {push,clone,fetch} can now spawn an external git subprocess, via\nthe git.subprocess = true config knob. This provides an alternative that,\nwhen turned on, fixes SSH bugs when interacting with Git remotes due to\nlibgit2s limitations #4979."},"3671":{"id":"/changelog-640","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj describe now accepts --edit."},"3672":{"id":"/changelog-641","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj evolog and jj op log now accept --reversed."},"3673":{"id":"/changelog-642","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj restore now supports -i/--interactive selection."},"3674":{"id":"/changelog-643","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj file list now supports templating."},"3675":{"id":"/changelog-644","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"There is a new builtin_op_log_oneline template alias you can pass to jj op\nlog -T for a more compact output. You can use format_operation_oneline and\nformat_snapshot_operation_oneline to customize parts of it."},"3676":{"id":"/changelog-645","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New template function config(name) to access to configuration variable from\ntemplate."},"3677":{"id":"/changelog-646","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New template function pad_centered() to center content within a minimum\nwidth."},"3678":{"id":"/changelog-647","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"Templater now supports list.filter(|x| ..) method."},"3679":{"id":"/changelog-648","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"The diff commit template keyword now supports custom formatting via\ndiff.files(). For example, diff.files().map(|e| e.path().display()) prints\nchanged file paths."},"3680":{"id":"/changelog-649","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"The diff.stat() template method now provides methods to get summary values."},"3681":{"id":"/changelog-650","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj log can now show cryptographic commit signatures. The output can be\ncontrolled by the ui.show-cryptographic-signatures=true config knob. The\nsignature template can be customized using\nformat_detailed_cryptographic_signature(signature) and\nformat_short_cryptographic_signature(signature)."},"3682":{"id":"/changelog-651","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New git.sign-on-push config option to automatically sign commits which are\nbeing pushed to a Git remote."},"3683":{"id":"/changelog-652","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New git.push-new-bookmarks config option to push new bookmarks without\n--allow-new."},"3684":{"id":"/changelog-653","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"jj status now shows untracked files when they reside directly under a\ntracked directory. There's still an issue that files under untracked\ndirectories aren't listed. #5389"},"3685":{"id":"/changelog-654","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.diff-expected-exit-codes config option to suppress\nwarnings from tools exiting with non-zero exit codes."},"3686":{"id":"/changelog-655","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New fix.tools.TOOL.enabled config option to enable/disable tools. This is\nuseful for defining disabled tools in user configuration that can be enabled\nin individual repositories with one config setting."},"3687":{"id":"/changelog-656","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"Added --into flag to jj restore, similarly to jj squash and jj\nabsorb. It is equivalent to --to, but --into is the recommended name."},"3688":{"id":"/changelog-657","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"Italic text is now supported. You can set e.g. colors.error = { fg = \"red\",\nitalic = true } in your config."},"3689":{"id":"/changelog-658","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New author_name/author_email/committer_name/committer_email(pattern)\nrevset functions to match either name or email field explicitly."},"3690":{"id":"/changelog-659","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"New subject(pattern) revset function that matches first line of commit\ndescriptions."},"3691":{"id":"/changelog-660","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"Conditional configuration now supports --when.commands to change\nconfiguration based on subcommand."},"3692":{"id":"/changelog-661","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-8","content":"The Jujutsu documentation site now publishes a schema for the official\nconfiguration file, which can be integrated into your editor for autocomplete,\ninline errors, and more.\nPlease see the documentation for more\non this."},"3693":{"id":"/changelog-662","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"jj git fetch with multiple remotes will now fetch from all remotes before\nimporting refs into the jj repo. This fixes a race condition where the\ntreatment of a commit that is found in multiple fetch remotes depended on the\norder the remotes were specified."},"3694":{"id":"/changelog-663","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"Fixed diff selection by external tools with jj split/commit -i FILESETS.\n#5252"},"3695":{"id":"/changelog-664","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"Conditional configuration now applies when initializing new repository.\n#5144"},"3696":{"id":"/changelog-665","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"[diff.<format>] configuration now applies to .diff().<format>() commit\ntemplate methods."},"3697":{"id":"/changelog-666","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"Conflicts at the end of files which don't end with a newline character are\nnow materialized in a way that can be parsed correctly.\n#3968"},"3698":{"id":"/changelog-667","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-10","content":"Bookmark and remote names written by jj git clone to\nrevset-aliases.'trunk()' are now escaped if necessary.\n#5359"},"3699":{"id":"/changelog-668","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3700":{"id":"/changelog-669","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Angel Ezquerra (@AngelEzquerra)"},"3701":{"id":"/changelog-670","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Antoine Martin (@alarsyo)"},"3702":{"id":"/changelog-671","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Anton Bulakh (@necauqua)"},"3703":{"id":"/changelog-672","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3704":{"id":"/changelog-673","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Baltasar 