"page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3719":{"id":"/changelog-688","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Matt Kulukundis (@fowles)"},"3720":{"id":"/changelog-689","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Ollivier Robert (@keltia)"},"3721":{"id":"/changelog-690","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3722":{"id":"/changelog-691","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Philipp Albrecht (@pylbrecht)"},"3723":{"id":"/changelog-692","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Robert Jackson (@rwjblue)"},"3724":{"id":"/changelog-693","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Samuel Tardieu (@samueltardieu)"},"3725":{"id":"/changelog-694","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3726":{"id":"/changelog-695","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"3727":{"id":"/changelog-696","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Valentin Gatien-Baron (@v-gb)"},"3728":{"id":"/changelog-697","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3729":{"id":"/changelog-698","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Waleed Khan (@arxanas)"},"3730":{"id":"/changelog-699","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-8","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3731":{"id":"/changelog-700","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-6","content":"It's the holidays, and this release was overall pretty quiet, without many major\nchanges. Two select improvements:"},"3732":{"id":"/changelog-701","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-6","content":"Improvements to configuration management, including support for conditional\nvariables in config files."},"3733":{"id":"/changelog-702","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-6","content":"Large files in the working copy will no longer cause commands to fail; instead\nthe large files will remain intact but untracked in the working copy."},"3734":{"id":"/changelog-703","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"Configuration variables are no longer \"stringly\" typed. For example, true is\nnot converted to a string \"true\", and vice versa."},"3735":{"id":"/changelog-704","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"The following configuration variables are now parsed strictly:\ncolors.<labels>, git.abandon-unreachable-commits,\ngit.auto-local-bookmark, git.push-bookmark-prefix, revsets.log,\nrevsets.short-prefixes, signing.backend, operation.hostname,\noperation.username, ui.allow-init-native, ui.color,\nui.default-description, ui.progress-indicator, ui.quiet, user.email,\nuser.name"},"3736":{"id":"/changelog-705","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"jj config list now prints inline tables { key = value, .. } literally.\nInner items of inline tables are no longer merged across configuration files.\nSee the table syntax\ndocumentation for\ndetails."},"3737":{"id":"/changelog-706","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"jj config edit --user now opens a file even if $JJ_CONFIG points to a\ndirectory. If there are multiple config files, the command will fail."},"3738":{"id":"/changelog-707","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"jj config set no longer accepts a bare string value that looks like a TOML\nexpression. For example, jj config set NAME '[foo]' must be quoted as jj\nconfig set NAME '\"[foo]\"'."},"3739":{"id":"/changelog-708","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"The deprecated [alias] config section is no longer respected. Move command\naliases to the [aliases] section."},"3740":{"id":"/changelog-709","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-9","content":"jj absorb now abandons the source commit if it becomes empty and has no\ndescription."},"3741":{"id":"/changelog-710","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-9","content":"--config-toml=TOML is deprecated in favor of --config=NAME=VALUE and\n--config-file=PATH."},"3742":{"id":"/changelog-711","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-9","content":"The Signature.username() template method is deprecated for\nSignature.email().local()."},"3743":{"id":"/changelog-712","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"jj command no longer fails due to new working-copy files larger than the\nsnapshot.max-new-file-size config option. It will print a warning and large\nfiles will be left untracked."},"3744":{"id":"/changelog-713","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"Configuration files now support conditional\nvariables."},"3745":{"id":"/changelog-714","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"New command options --config=NAME=VALUE and --config-file=PATH to set\nstring value without quoting and to load additional configuration from files."},"3746":{"id":"/changelog-715","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"Templates now support the >=, >, <=, and < relational operators for\nInteger types."},"3747":{"id":"/changelog-716","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"A new Email template type is added. Signature.email() now returns an Email\ntemplate type instead of a String."},"3748":{"id":"/changelog-717","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"Adds a new template alias commit_timestamp(commit) which defaults to the\ncommitter date."},"3749":{"id":"/changelog-718","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"Conflict markers are now allowed to be longer than 7 characters, allowing\nconflicts to be materialized and parsed correctly in files which already\ncontain lines that look like conflict markers."},"3750":{"id":"/changelog-719","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"New $marker_length variable to allow merge tools to support longer conflict\nmarkers (equivalent to \"%L\" for Git merge drivers)."},"3751":{"id":"/changelog-720","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-9","content":"jj describe now accepts a JJ: ignore-rest line that ignores everything\nbelow it, similar to a \"scissor line\" in git. When editing multiple commits,\nonly ignore until the next JJ: describe line."},"3752":{"id":"/changelog-721","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"The $NO_COLOR environment variable must now be non-empty to be respected."},"3753":{"id":"/changelog-722","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"Fixed incompatible rendering of empty hunks in git/unified diffs.\n#5049"},"3754":{"id":"/changelog-723","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"Fixed performance of progress bar rendering when fetching from Git remote.\n#5057"},"3755":{"id":"/changelog-724","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"jj config path --user no longer creates new file at the default config path."},"3756":{"id":"/changelog-725","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"On Windows, workspace paths (printed by jj root) no longer use UNC-style\n\\\\?\\ paths unless necessary."},"3757":{"id":"/changelog-726","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"On Windows, jj git clone now converts local Git remote path to\nslash-separated path."},"3758":{"id":"/changelog-727","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-11","content":"jj resolve no longer removes the executable bit on resolved files when using\nan external merge tool."},"3759":{"id":"/changelog-728","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3760":{"id":"/changelog-729","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Alex Stefanov (@umnikos)"},"3761":{"id":"/changelog-730","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Anton Älgmyr (@algmyr)"},"3762":{"id":"/changelog-731","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3763":{"id":"/changelog-732","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3764":{"id":"/changelog-733","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Bryce Berger (@bryceberger)"},"3765":{"id":"/changelog-734","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"3766":{"id":"/changelog-735","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"David Crespo (@david-crespo)"},"3767":{"id":"/changelog-736","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"George Tsiamasiotis (@gtsiam)"},"3768":{"id":"/changelog-737","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Jochen Kupperschmidt (@homeworkprod)"},"3769":{"id":"/changelog-738","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Keane Nguyen (@keanemind)"},"3770":{"id":"/changelog-739","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3771":{"id":"/changelog-740","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Matt Kulukundis (@fowles)"},"3772":{"id":"/changelog-741","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Milo Moisson (@mrnossiom)"},"3773":{"id":"/changelog-742","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"petricavalry (@petricavalry)"},"3774":{"id":"/changelog-743","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3775":{"id":"/changelog-744","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Remo Senekowitsch (@senekor)"},"3776":{"id":"/changelog-745","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3777":{"id":"/changelog-746","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Shane Sveller (@shanesveller)"},"3778":{"id":"/changelog-747","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"3779":{"id":"/changelog-748","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Tim Janik (@tim-janik)"},"3780":{"id":"/changelog-749","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Vamsi Avula (@avamsi)"},"3781":{"id":"/changelog-750","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Waleed Khan (@arxanas)"},"3782":{"id":"/changelog-751","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-9","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3783":{"id":"/changelog-752","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-7","content":"New jj absorb command automatically squashes changes from the current commit into relevant ancestor commits."},"3784":{"id":"/changelog-753","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-7","content":"Experimental dynamic shell completions have been added; see the docs for configuration."},"3785":{"id":"/changelog-754","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-7","content":"jj duplicate now accepts --destination/--insert-before/--insert-after."},"3786":{"id":"/changelog-755","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#release-highlights-7","content":"Some deprecated commands have been removed (jj move, jj checkout, jj merge)."},"3787":{"id":"/changelog-756","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-10","content":"jj move has been removed. It was deprecated in 0.16.0."},"3788":{"id":"/changelog-757","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-10","content":"jj checkout and the built-in alias jj co have been removed.\nIt was deprecated in 0.14.0."},"3789":{"id":"/changelog-758","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-10","content":"jj merge has been removed. It was deprecated in 0.14.0."},"3790":{"id":"/changelog-759","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-10","content":"jj git push no longer pushes new bookmarks by default. Use --allow-new to\nbypass this restriction."},"3791":{"id":"/changelog-760","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-10","content":"Lines prefixed with \"JJ:\" in commit descriptions and in sparse patterns (from\njj sparse edit) are now stripped even if they are not immediately followed\nby a space. #5004"},"3792":{"id":"/changelog-761","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"Templates now support the == and != logical operators for Boolean,\nInteger, and String types."},"3793":{"id":"/changelog-762","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New command jj absorb that moves changes to stack of mutable revisions."},"3794":{"id":"/changelog-763","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New command jj util exec that can be used for arbitrary aliases."},"3795":{"id":"/changelog-764","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"jj rebase -b can now be used with the --insert-after and --insert-before\noptions, like jj rebase -r and jj rebase -s."},"3796":{"id":"/changelog-765","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"A preview of improved shell completions was added. Please refer to the\ndocumentation\nto activate them. They additionally complete context-dependent, dynamic values\nlike bookmarks, aliases, revisions, operations and files."},"3797":{"id":"/changelog-766","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"Added the config setting snapshot.auto-update-stale for automatically\nrunning jj workspace update-stale when applicable."},"3798":{"id":"/changelog-767","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"jj duplicate now accepts --destination, --insert-after and\n--insert-before options to customize the location of the duplicated\nrevisions."},"3799":{"id":"/changelog-768","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"jj log now displays the working-copy branch first."},"3800":{"id":"/changelog-769","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New fork_point() revset function can be used to obtain the fork point\nof multiple commits."},"3801":{"id":"/changelog-770","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"The tags() revset function now takes an optional pattern argument,\nmirroring that of bookmarks()."},"3802":{"id":"/changelog-771","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"Several commands now support -f/-t shorthands for --from/--to:"},"3803":{"id":"/changelog-772","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"diff"},"3804":{"id":"/changelog-773","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"diffedit"},"3805":{"id":"/changelog-774","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"interdiff"},"3806":{"id":"/changelog-775","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"op diff"},"3807":{"id":"/changelog-776","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"restore"},"3808":{"id":"/changelog-777","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New ui.conflict-marker-style config option to change how conflicts are\nmaterialized in the working copy. The default option (\"diff\") renders\nconflicts as a snapshot with a list of diffs to apply to the snapshot.\nThe new \"snapshot\" option renders conflicts as a series of snapshots, showing\neach side and base of the conflict. The new \"git\" option replicates Git's\n\"diff3\" conflict style, meaning it is more likely to work with external tools,\nbut it doesn't support conflicts with more than 2 sides."},"3809":{"id":"/changelog-778","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.conflict-marker-style config option to override the\nconflict marker style used for a specific merge tool."},"3810":{"id":"/changelog-779","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.merge-conflict-exit-codes config option to allow a\nmerge tool to exit with a non-zero code to indicate that not all conflicts\nwere resolved."},"3811":{"id":"/changelog-780","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-10","content":"jj simplify-parents now supports configuring the default revset when no\n--source or --revisions arguments are provided with the\nrevsets.simplify-parents config."},"3812":{"id":"/changelog-781","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-12","content":"jj config unset <TABLE-NAME> no longer removes a table (such as [ui].)"},"3813":{"id":"/changelog-782","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3814":{"id":"/changelog-783","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3815":{"id":"/changelog-784","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3816":{"id":"/changelog-785","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"3817":{"id":"/changelog-786","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Emily (@neongreen)"},"3818":{"id":"/changelog-787","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Essien Ita Essien (@essiene)"},"3819":{"id":"/changelog-788","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Herman J. Radtke III (@hjr3)"},"3820":{"id":"/changelog-789","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3821":{"id":"/changelog-790","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Joaquín Triñanes (@JoaquinTrinanes)"},"3822":{"id":"/changelog-791","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Lars Francke (@lfrancke)"},"3823":{"id":"/changelog-792","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Luke Randall (@lukerandall)"},"3824":{"id":"/changelog-793","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3825":{"id":"/changelog-794","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Nathanael Huffman (@nathanaelhuffman)"},"3826":{"id":"/changelog-795","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3827":{"id":"/changelog-796","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Remo Senekowitsch (@senekor)"},"3828":{"id":"/changelog-797","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Robin Stocker (@robinst)"},"3829":{"id":"/changelog-798","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3830":{"id":"/changelog-799","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Shane Sveller (@shanesveller)"},"3831":{"id":"/changelog-800","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Tim Janik (@tim-janik)"},"3832":{"id":"/changelog-801","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-10","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3833":{"id":"/changelog-802","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#security-fixes-1","content":"Fixed path traversal by cloning/checking out crafted Git repository containing\n.., .jj, .git paths.\n(GHSA-88h5-6w7m-5w56;CVE-2024-51990)"},"3834":{"id":"/changelog-803","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"Revset function names can no longer start with a number."},"3835":{"id":"/changelog-804","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"Evaluation error of revsets.short-prefixes configuration is now reported."},"3836":{"id":"/changelog-805","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"The HEAD@git symbol no longer resolves to the Git HEAD revision. Use\ngit_head() or @- revset expression instead. The git_head template\nkeyword now returns a boolean."},"3837":{"id":"/changelog-806","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"Help command doesn't work recursively anymore, i.e. jj workspace help root\ndoesn't work anymore."},"3838":{"id":"/changelog-807","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"The color label op_log from the [colors] config section now only\napplies to the op log and not to the other places operations are displayed. In\nalmost all cases, if you configured op_log before, you should use the new\noperation label instead."},"3839":{"id":"/changelog-808","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-11","content":"Default operation log template now shows end times of operations instead of\nstart times."},"3840":{"id":"/changelog-809","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-11","content":"git.auto-local-bookmark replaces git.auto-local-branch. The latter remains\nsupported for now (at lower precedence than the former)."},"3841":{"id":"/changelog-810","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"Added diff options to ignore whitespace when comparing lines. Whitespace\nchanges are still highlighted."},"3842":{"id":"/changelog-811","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New command jj simplify-parents will remove redundant parent edges."},"3843":{"id":"/changelog-812","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"jj squash now supports -f/-t shorthands for --from/--[in]to."},"3844":{"id":"/changelog-813","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"Initial support for shallow Git repositories has been implemented. However,\ndeepening the history of a shallow repository is not yet supported."},"3845":{"id":"/changelog-814","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"jj git clone now accepts a --depth <DEPTH> option, which\nallows to clone the repository with a given depth."},"3846":{"id":"/changelog-815","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New command jj file annotate that annotates files line by line. This is similar\nin functionality to git blame. Invoke the command with jj file annotate <file_path>.\nThe output can be customized via the templates.annotate_commit_summary\nconfig variable."},"3847":{"id":"/changelog-816","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"jj bookmark list gained a --remote REMOTE option to display bookmarks\nbelonging to a remote. This option can be combined with --tracked or\n--conflicted."},"3848":{"id":"/changelog-817","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New command jj config unset that unsets config values. For example,\njj config unset --user user.name."},"3849":{"id":"/changelog-818","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"jj help now has the flag --keyword (shorthand -k), which can give help\nfor some keywords (e.g. jj help -k revsets). To see a list of the available\nkeywords you can do jj help --help."},"3850":{"id":"/changelog-819","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New at_operation(op, expr) revset can be used in order to query revisions\nbased on historical state."},"3851":{"id":"/changelog-820","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"String literals in filesets, revsets and templates now support hex bytes\n(with \\e as escape / shorthand for \\x1b)."},"3852":{"id":"/changelog-821","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New coalesce(revsets...) revset which returns commits in the first revset\nin the revsets list that does not evaluate to none()."},"3853":{"id":"/changelog-822","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New template function raw_escape_sequence(...) preserves escape sequences."},"3854":{"id":"/changelog-823","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"Timestamp objects in templates now have after(date) -> Boolean and\nbefore(date) -> Boolean methods for comparing timestamps to other dates."},"3855":{"id":"/changelog-824","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"New template functions pad_start(), pad_end(), truncate_start(), and\ntruncate_end() are added."},"3856":{"id":"/changelog-825","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"Add a new template alias builtin_log_compact_full_description()."},"3857":{"id":"/changelog-826","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-11","content":"Added the config settings diff.color-words.context and diff.git.context to\ncontrol the default number of lines of context shown."},"3858":{"id":"/changelog-827","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-13","content":"Error on trunk() revset resolution is now handled gracefully.\n#4616"},"3859":{"id":"/changelog-828","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-13","content":"Updated the built-in diff editor scm-record to version\n0.4.0, which\nincludes multiple fixes."},"3860":{"id":"/changelog-829","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3861":{"id":"/changelog-830","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Alec Snyder (@allonsy)"},"3862":{"id":"/changelog-831","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Arthur Grillo (Grillo-0)"},"3863":{"id":"/changelog-832","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3864":{"id":"/changelog-833","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3865":{"id":"/changelog-834","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Dave Townsend (@Mossop)"},"3866":{"id":"/changelog-835","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"3867":{"id":"/changelog-836","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Emily (@neongreen)"},"3868":{"id":"/changelog-837","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Essien Ita Essien (@essiene)"},"3869":{"id":"/changelog-838","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Fedor Sheremetyev (@sheremetyev)"},"3870":{"id":"/changelog-839","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3871":{"id":"/changelog-840","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Jakub Okoński (@farnoy)"},"3872":{"id":"/changelog-841","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Jcparkyn (@Jcparkyn)"},"3873":{"id":"/changelog-842","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Joaquín Triñanes (@JoaquinTrinanes)"},"3874":{"id":"/changelog-843","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Lukas Wirth (@Veykril)"},"3875":{"id":"/changelog-844","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Marco Neumann (@crepererum)"},"3876":{"id":"/changelog-845","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3877":{"id":"/changelog-846","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Matt Stark (@matts1)"},"3878":{"id":"/changelog-847","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3879":{"id":"/changelog-848","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Philipp Albrecht (@pylbrecht)"},"3880":{"id":"/changelog-849","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Remo Senekowitsch (@senekor)"},"3881":{"id":"/changelog-850","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Richard Macklin (@rmacklin)"},"3882":{"id":"/changelog-851","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Robin Stocker (@robinst)"},"3883":{"id":"/changelog-852","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Samuel Tardieu (@samueltardieu)"},"3884":{"id":"/changelog-853","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Sora (@SoraTenshi)"},"3885":{"id":"/changelog-854","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"3886":{"id":"/changelog-855","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Theodore Ehrenborg (@TheodoreEhrenborg)"},"3887":{"id":"/changelog-856","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Vamsi Avula (@avamsi)"},"3888":{"id":"/changelog-857","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Vincent Ging Ho Yim (@cenviity)"},"3889":{"id":"/changelog-858","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-11","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3890":{"id":"/changelog-859","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-12","content":"Fixing #4239 means the\nordering of some messages have changed."},"3891":{"id":"/changelog-860","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-12","content":"Invalid ui.graph.style configuration is now an error."},"3892":{"id":"/changelog-861","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-12","content":"The builtin template branch_list has been renamed to bookmark_list as part\nof the jj branch deprecation."},"3893":{"id":"/changelog-862","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"jj branch has been deprecated in favor of jj bookmark."},"3894":{"id":"/changelog-863","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"Rationale: Jujutsu's branches don't behave like Git branches, which a\nconfused many newcomers, as they expected a similar behavior given the name.\nWe've renamed them to \"bookmarks\" to match the actual behavior, as we think\nthat describes them better, and they also behave similar to Mercurial's\nbookmarks."},"3895":{"id":"/changelog-864","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"jj obslog is now called jj evolution-log/jj evolog. jj obslog remains\nas an alias."},"3896":{"id":"/changelog-865","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"jj unsquash has been deprecated in favor of jj squash and\njj diffedit --restore-descendants."},"3897":{"id":"/changelog-866","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"Rationale: jj squash can be used in interactive mode to pull\nchanges from one commit to another, including from a parent commit\nto a child commit. For fine-grained dependent diffs, such as when\nthe parent and the child commits must successively modify the same\nlocation in a file, jj diffedit --restore-descendants can be used\nto set the parent commit to the desired content without altering the\ncontent of the child commit."},"3898":{"id":"/changelog-867","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"The git.push-branch-prefix config has been deprecated in favor of\ngit.push-bookmark-prefix."},"3899":{"id":"/changelog-868","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-12","content":"conflict() and file() revsets have been renamed to conflicts() and files()\nrespectively. The old names are still around and will be removed in a future\nrelease."},"3900":{"id":"/changelog-869","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"The new config option snapshot.auto-track lets you automatically track only\nthe specified paths (all paths by default). Use the new jj file track\ncommand to manually tracks path that were not automatically tracked. There is\nno way to list untracked files yet. Use git status in a colocated workspace\nas a workaround.\n#323"},"3901":{"id":"/changelog-870","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj fix now allows fixing unchanged files with the --include-unchanged-files flag. This\ncan be used to more easily introduce automatic formatting changes in a new\ncommit separate from other changes."},"3902":{"id":"/changelog-871","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj workspace add now accepts a --sparse-patterns=<MODE> option, which\nallows control of the sparse patterns for a newly created workspace: copy\n(inherit from parent; default), full (full working copy), or empty (the\nempty working copy)."},"3903":{"id":"/changelog-872","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"New command jj workspace rename that can rename the current workspace."},"3904":{"id":"/changelog-873","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj op log gained an option to include operation diffs."},"3905":{"id":"/changelog-874","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj git clone now accepts a --remote <REMOTE NAME> option, which\nallows to set a name for the remote instead of using the default\norigin."},"3906":{"id":"/changelog-875","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj op undo now reports information on the operation that has been undone."},"3907":{"id":"/changelog-876","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj squash: the -k flag can be used as a shorthand for --keep-emptied."},"3908":{"id":"/changelog-877","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"CommitId / ChangeId template types now support .normal_hex()."},"3909":{"id":"/changelog-878","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj commit and jj describe now accept --author option allowing to quickly change\nauthor of given commit."},"3910":{"id":"/changelog-879","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj diffedit, jj abandon, and jj restore now accept a --restore-descendants\nflag. When used, descendants of the edited or deleted commits will keep their original\ncontent."},"3911":{"id":"/changelog-880","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj git fetch -b <remote-git-branch-name> will now warn if the branch(es)\ncan not be found in any of the specified/configured remotes."},"3912":{"id":"/changelog-881","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"jj split now lets the user select all changes in interactive mode. This may be used\nto keeping all changes into the first commit while keeping the current commit\ndescription for the second commit (the newly created empty one)."},"3913":{"id":"/changelog-882","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-12","content":"Author and committer names are now yellow by default."},"3914":{"id":"/changelog-883","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-14","content":"Update working copy before reporting changes. This prevents errors during reporting\nfrom leaving the working copy in a stale state."},"3915":{"id":"/changelog-884","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-14","content":"Fixed panic when parsing invalid conflict markers of a particular form.\n(#2611)"},"3916":{"id":"/changelog-885","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-14","content":"Editing a hidden commit now makes it visible."},"3917":{"id":"/changelog-886","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-14","content":"The present() revset now suppresses missing working copy error. For example,\npresent(@) evaluates to none() if the current workspace has no\nworking-copy commit."},"3918":{"id":"/changelog-887","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3919":{"id":"/changelog-888","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3920":{"id":"/changelog-889","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Danny Hooper (@hooper)"},"3921":{"id":"/changelog-890","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Emily Shaffer (@nasamuffin)"},"3922":{"id":"/changelog-891","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Essien Ita Essien (@essiene)"},"3923":{"id":"/changelog-892","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Ethan Brierley (@eopb)"},"3924":{"id":"/changelog-893","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3925":{"id":"/changelog-894","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Kevin Liao (@kevincliao)"},"3926":{"id":"/changelog-895","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Lukas Wirth (@Veykril)"},"3927":{"id":"/changelog-896","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3928":{"id":"/changelog-897","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Mateusz Mikuła (@mati865)"},"3929":{"id":"/changelog-898","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"mlcui (@mlcui-corp)"},"3930":{"id":"/changelog-899","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"3931":{"id":"/changelog-900","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Samuel Tardieu (@samueltardieu)"},"3932":{"id":"/changelog-901","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"3933":{"id":"/changelog-902","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Tyler Goffinet (@qubitz)"},"3934":{"id":"/changelog-903","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Vamsi Avula (@avamsi)"},"3935":{"id":"/changelog-904","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-12","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3936":{"id":"/changelog-905","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-13","content":"next/prev will no longer infer when to go into edit mode when moving from\ncommit to commit. It now either follows the flags --edit|--no-edit or it\ngets the mode from ui.movement.edit."},"3937":{"id":"/changelog-906","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-13","content":"jj untrack has been renamed to jj file untrack."},"3938":{"id":"/changelog-907","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"Add new boolean config knob, ui.movement.edit for controlling the behavior\nof prev/next. The flag turns edit mode on and off permanently when set\nrespectively to true or false."},"3939":{"id":"/changelog-908","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"All diff formats except --name-only now include information about copies and\nmoves. So do external diff tools in file-by-file mode. jj status also\nincludes information about copies and moves."},"3940":{"id":"/changelog-909","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"Color-words diff has gained an option to display complex changes as separate\nlines. It's enabled by default. To\nrestore the old behavior, set diff.color-words.max-inline-alternation = -1."},"3941":{"id":"/changelog-910","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"A tilde (~) at the start of the path will now be expanded to the user's home\ndirectory when configuring a signing.key for SSH commit signing."},"3942":{"id":"/changelog-911","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"When reconfiguring the author, warn that the working copy won't be updated"},"3943":{"id":"/changelog-912","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-13","content":"jj rebase -s can now be used with the --insert-after and --insert-before\noptions, like jj rebase -r."},"3944":{"id":"/changelog-913","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-15","content":"Release binaries for Intel Macs have been restored. They were previously\nbroken due to using a sunset version of GitHub's macOS runners (but nobody had\npreviously complained.)"},"3945":{"id":"/changelog-914","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"3946":{"id":"/changelog-915","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Aaron Bull Schaefer (@elasticdog)"},"3947":{"id":"/changelog-916","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"3948":{"id":"/changelog-917","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"3949":{"id":"/changelog-918","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Raniz Daniel Raneland (@Raniz85)"},"3950":{"id":"/changelog-919","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"3951":{"id":"/changelog-920","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Essien Ita Essien (@essiene)"},"3952":{"id":"/changelog-921","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"3953":{"id":"/changelog-922","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Kaleb Pace (@kalebpace)"},"3954":{"id":"/changelog-923","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Marie (@NyCodeGHG)"},"3955":{"id":"/changelog-924","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Marijan Smetko (@InCogNiTo124)"},"3956":{"id":"/changelog-925","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"3957":{"id":"/changelog-926","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Matt Kulukundis (@fowles)"},"3958":{"id":"/changelog-927","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"3959":{"id":"/changelog-928","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"3960":{"id":"/changelog-929","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"tingerrr (@tingerrr)"},"3961":{"id":"/changelog-930","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-13","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"3962":{"id":"/changelog-931","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#note-to-packagers","content":"jj now links libgit2 statically by default. To use dynamic linking, you\nneed to set the environment variable LIBGIT2_NO_VENDOR=1 while compiling.\n(#4163)"},"3963":{"id":"/changelog-932","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"jj rebase --skip-empty has been renamed to jj rebase --skip-emptied"},"3964":{"id":"/changelog-933","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"jj backout --revision has been renamed to jj backout --revisions.\nThe short alias -r is still supported."},"3965":{"id":"/changelog-934","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"The default immutable_heads() set\nnow includes untracked_remote_branches() with the assumption that untracked\nbranches aren't managed by you. Therefore, untracked branches are no longer\ndisplayed in jj log by default."},"3966":{"id":"/changelog-935","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"Updated defaults for graph node symbol templates templates.log_node and\ntemplates.op_log_node."},"3967":{"id":"/changelog-936","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"The \"fileset\" language is now enabled by default. It can\nstill be disabled by setting ui.allow-filesets=false."},"3968":{"id":"/changelog-937","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"On jj git fetch/import, commits referred to by HEAD@git are no longer\npreserved. If a checked-out named branch gets deleted locally or remotely, the\ncorresponding commits will be abandoned."},"3969":{"id":"/changelog-938","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"jj --at-op=@ no longer merges concurrent operations if explicitly specified."},"3970":{"id":"/changelog-939","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-14","content":"jj obslog -p no longer shows diffs at non-partial squash operations.\nPreviously, it showed the same diffs as the second predecessor."},"3971":{"id":"/changelog-940","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-14","content":"The original configuration syntax for jj fix is now deprecated in favor of\none that allows defining multiple tools that can affect different filesets.\nThese can be used in combination for now. See jj help fix for details."},"3972":{"id":"/changelog-941","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"Define immutable_heads() revset alias in terms of a new builtin_immutable_heads().\nThis enables users to redefine immutable_heads() as they wish, but still\nhave builtin_immutable_heads() which should not be redefined."},"3973":{"id":"/changelog-942","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"External diff tools can now be configured to invoke the tool on each file\nindividually instead of being passed a directory by setting\nmerge-tools.$TOOL.diff-invocation-mode=\"file-by-file\" in config.toml."},"3974":{"id":"/changelog-943","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"In git diffs, word-level hunks are now highlighted with underline. See diff\ncolors and styles for customization."},"3975":{"id":"/changelog-944","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New .diff().<format>() commit template methods are added. They can be used\nin order to show diffs conditionally. For example,\nif(current_working_copy, diff.summary())."},"3976":{"id":"/changelog-945","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"jj git clone and jj git init with an existing git repository adds the\ndefault branch of the remote as repository settings for\nrevset-aliases.\"trunk()\".`"},"3977":{"id":"/changelog-946","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"jj workspace forget now abandons the workspace's working-copy commit if it\nwas empty."},"3978":{"id":"/changelog-947","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"jj backout now includes the backed out commit's subject in the new commit\nmessage."},"3979":{"id":"/changelog-948","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"jj backout can now back out multiple commits at once."},"3980":{"id":"/changelog-949","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"jj git clone some/nested/path now creates the full directory tree for\nnested destination paths if they don't exist."},"3981":{"id":"/changelog-950","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"String patterns now support case‐insensitive matching by suffixing any\npattern kind with -i. mine() uses case‐insensitive matching on your email\naddress unconditionally. Only ASCII case folding is currently implemented,\nbut this will likely change in the future."},"3982":{"id":"/changelog-951","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"String patterns now support regex:\"pattern\"."},"3983":{"id":"/changelog-952","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New tracked_remote_branches() and untracked_remote_branches() revset\nfunctions can be used to select tracked/untracked remote branches."},"3984":{"id":"/changelog-953","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"The file() revset function now accepts fileset as argument."},"3985":{"id":"/changelog-954","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New diff_contains() revset function can be used to search diffs."},"3986":{"id":"/changelog-955","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New command jj operation diff that can compare changes made between two\noperations."},"3987":{"id":"/changelog-956","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New command jj operation show that can show the changes made in a single\noperation."},"3988":{"id":"/changelog-957","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"New config setting git.private-commits to prevent commits from being pushed."},"3989":{"id":"/changelog-958","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-14","content":"The default commit description template\ncan now be configured by templates.draft_commit_description."},"3990":{"id":"/change