ors-15","content":"Manuel Caldeira (@KiitoX)"},"4065":{"id":"/changelog-1034","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"4066":{"id":"/changelog-1035","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Matt Kulukundis (@fowles)"},"4067":{"id":"/changelog-1036","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Matt Stark (@matts1)"},"4068":{"id":"/changelog-1037","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"mlcui (@mlcui-corp)"},"4069":{"id":"/changelog-1038","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"4070":{"id":"/changelog-1039","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Scott Taylor (@scott2000)"},"4071":{"id":"/changelog-1040","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Simon Wollwage (@Kintaro)"},"4072":{"id":"/changelog-1041","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Tal Pressman (@tp-woven)"},"4073":{"id":"/changelog-1042","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-15","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"4074":{"id":"/changelog-1043","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"Dropped support for ui.default-revset config (replaced by revsets.log in\n0.8.0)."},"4075":{"id":"/changelog-1044","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"The commit_summary_no_branches template is superseded by\ntemplates.branch_list."},"4076":{"id":"/changelog-1045","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"jj split will now refuse to split an empty commit."},"4077":{"id":"/changelog-1046","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"jj config list now uses multi-line strings and single-quoted strings in the\noutput when appropriate."},"4078":{"id":"/changelog-1047","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"jj config get/list/set now parse name argument as TOML\nkey. Quote meta characters as needed.\nExample: jj config get \"revset-aliases.'trunk()'\""},"4079":{"id":"/changelog-1048","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"When updating the working copy away from an empty and undescribed commit, it\nis now abandoned even if it is a merge commit."},"4080":{"id":"/changelog-1049","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"If a new working-copy commit is created because the old one was abandoned, and\nthe old commit was merge, then the new commit will now also be.\n#2859"},"4081":{"id":"/changelog-1050","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-16","content":"jj new's --insert-before/--insert-after options must now be set for each\ncommit the new commit will be inserted before/after. Previously, those options\nwere global flags and specifying them once would insert the new commit before/\nafter all the specified commits."},"4082":{"id":"/changelog-1051","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-16","content":"Attempting to alias a built-in command now gives a warning, rather than being\nsilently ignored."},"4083":{"id":"/changelog-1052","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"jj branch list/tag list now accept -T/--template option. The tag list\nprints commit summary along with the tag name by default."},"4084":{"id":"/changelog-1053","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"Conflict markers now include an explanation of what each part of the conflict\nrepresents."},"4085":{"id":"/changelog-1054","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"ui.color = \"debug\" prints active labels alongside the regular colored\noutput."},"4086":{"id":"/changelog-1055","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"jj branch track now show conflicts if there are some."},"4087":{"id":"/changelog-1056","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"A new revset reachable(srcs, domain) will return all commits that are\nreachable from srcs within domain."},"4088":{"id":"/changelog-1057","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"There are now prebuilt binaries for aarch64-linux-unknown-musl.\nNote, these are cross compiled and currently untested.\nWe plan on providing fully tested builds later once our CI system allows it."},"4089":{"id":"/changelog-1058","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"Added new revsets mutable() and immutable()."},"4090":{"id":"/changelog-1059","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"Upgraded scm-record from v0.2.0 to v0.3.0. See release notes at\nhttps://github.com/arxanas/scm-record/releases/tag/v0.3.0"},"4091":{"id":"/changelog-1060","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"New command jj fix that can be configured to update commits by running code\nformatters (or similar tools) on changed files. The configuration schema and\nflags are minimal for now, with a number of improvements planned (for example,\n#3800 and\n#3801)."},"4092":{"id":"/changelog-1061","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"jj new's --insert-before and --insert-after options can now be used\nsimultaneously."},"4093":{"id":"/changelog-1062","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-16","content":"jj git push now can push commits with empty descriptions with the\n--allow-empty-description flag"},"4094":{"id":"/changelog-1063","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"Previously, jj git push only made sure that the branch is in the expected\nlocation on the remote server when pushing a branch forward (as opposed to\nsideways or backwards). Now, jj git push makes a safety check in all cases\nand fails whenever jj git fetch would have introduced a conflict."},"4095":{"id":"/changelog-1064","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"In other words, previously branches that moved sideways or backward were\npushed similarly to Git's git push --force; now they have protections\nsimilar to git push --force-with-lease (though not identical to it, to match\nthe behavior of jj git fetch). Note also that because of the way jj git\nfetch works, jj does not suffer from the same problems as Git's git push\n--force-with-lease in situations when git fetch is run in the background."},"4096":{"id":"/changelog-1065","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"When the working copy commit becomes immutable, a new one is automatically\ncreated\non top of it to avoid letting the user edit the immutable one."},"4097":{"id":"/changelog-1066","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"jj config list now properly escapes TOML keys (#1322)."},"4098":{"id":"/changelog-1067","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"Files with conflicts are now checked out as executable if all sides of the\nconflict are executable."},"4099":{"id":"/changelog-1068","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-18","content":"The progress bar (visible when using e.g. jj git clone) clears the\nremainder of the cursor row after drawing rather than clearing the entire row\nbefore drawing, eliminating the \"flicker\" effect seen on some terminals."},"4100":{"id":"/changelog-1069","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"4101":{"id":"/changelog-1070","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Alexander Potashev (@aspotashev)"},"4102":{"id":"/changelog-1071","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"4103":{"id":"/changelog-1072","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"4104":{"id":"/changelog-1073","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Charles Crete (@Cretezy)"},"4105":{"id":"/changelog-1074","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"4106":{"id":"/changelog-1075","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Danny Hooper (@hooper)"},"4107":{"id":"/changelog-1076","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Eidolon (@HybridEidolon)"},"4108":{"id":"/changelog-1077","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Glen Choo (@chooglen)"},"4109":{"id":"/changelog-1078","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Gregory Anders (@gpanders)"},"4110":{"id":"/changelog-1079","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"4111":{"id":"/changelog-1080","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"jyn (@jyn514)"},"4112":{"id":"/changelog-1081","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"4113":{"id":"/changelog-1082","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Matt Stark (@matts1)"},"4114":{"id":"/changelog-1083","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Matthew Davidson (@KingMob)"},"4115":{"id":"/changelog-1084","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Michael Gattozzi (@mgattozzi)"},"4116":{"id":"/changelog-1085","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"mlcui (@mlcui-corp)"},"4117":{"id":"/changelog-1086","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"4118":{"id":"/changelog-1087","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Remo Senekowitsch (@senekor)"},"4119":{"id":"/changelog-1088","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Thomas Castiglione (@gulbanana)"},"4120":{"id":"/changelog-1089","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Théo Daron (@tdaron)"},"4121":{"id":"/changelog-1090","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"tinger (@tingerrr)"},"4122":{"id":"/changelog-1091","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Waleed Khan (@arxanas)"},"4123":{"id":"/changelog-1092","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-16","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"4124":{"id":"/changelog-1093","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-19","content":"jj status no longer scans through the entire history to look for ancestors\nwith conflicts."},"4125":{"id":"/changelog-1094","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-17","content":"The default template aliases were replaced as follows:"},"4126":{"id":"/changelog-1095","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-17","content":"builtin_op_log_root(op_id: OperationId) ->\nformat_root_operation(root: Operation)"},"4127":{"id":"/changelog-1096","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-17","content":"builtin_log_root(change_id: ChangeId, commit_id: CommitId) ->\nformat_root_commit(root: Commit)"},"4128":{"id":"/changelog-1097","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-17","content":"builtin_change_id_with_hidden_and_divergent_info ->\nformat_short_change_id_with_hidden_and_divergent_info(commit: Commit)"},"4129":{"id":"/changelog-1098","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-17","content":"The --revision option of jj rebase is renamed to --revisions. The short\nalias -r is still supported."},"4130":{"id":"/changelog-1099","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"The list of conflicted paths is printed whenever the working copy changes.\nThis can be disabled with the --quiet option."},"4131":{"id":"/changelog-1100","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"Commit objects in templates now have a mine() -> Boolean method analog to\nthe same function in revsets. It evaluates to true if the email of the commit\nauthor matches the current user.email."},"4132":{"id":"/changelog-1101","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"Commit objects in templates now have a contained_in(revset: String) ->\nBoolean method."},"4133":{"id":"/changelog-1102","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"Operation objects in templates now have a snapshot() -> Boolean method that\nevaluates to true if the operation was a snapshot created by a non-mutating\ncommand (e.g. jj log)."},"4134":{"id":"/changelog-1103","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"Revsets and templates now support single-quoted raw string literals."},"4135":{"id":"/changelog-1104","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"A new config option ui.always-allow-large-revsets has been added to\nallow large revsets expressions in some commands, without the all: prefix."},"4136":{"id":"/changelog-1105","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"A new config option ui.allow-filesets has been added to enable \"fileset\"\nexpressions. Note that filesets are currently experimental,\nbut will be enabled by default in a future release."},"4137":{"id":"/changelog-1106","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"A new global flag --ignore-immutable lets you rewrite immutable commits."},"4138":{"id":"/changelog-1107","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"New command jj parallelize that rebases a set of revisions into siblings."},"4139":{"id":"/changelog-1108","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"jj status now supports filtering by paths. For example, jj status . will\nonly list changed files that are descendants of the current directory."},"4140":{"id":"/changelog-1109","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"jj prev and jj next now work when the working copy revision is a merge."},"4141":{"id":"/changelog-1110","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"jj squash now accepts a --use-destination-message/-u option that uses the\ndescription of the destination for the new squashed revision and discards the\ndescriptions of the source revisions."},"4142":{"id":"/changelog-1111","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"You can check whether Watchman fsmonitor is enabled or installed with the new\njj debug watchman status command."},"4143":{"id":"/changelog-1112","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"jj rebase now accepts revsets resolving to multiple revisions with the\n--revisions/-r option."},"4144":{"id":"/changelog-1113","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-17","content":"jj rebase -r now accepts --insert-after and --insert-before options to\ncustomize the location of the rebased revisions."},"4145":{"id":"/changelog-1114","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-20","content":"Revsets now support \\-escapes in string literal."},"4146":{"id":"/changelog-1115","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-20","content":"The builtin diff editor now allows empty files to be selected during\njj split."},"4147":{"id":"/changelog-1116","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-20","content":"Fixed a bug with jj split introduced in 0.16.0 that caused it to incorrectly\nrebase the children of the revision being split if they had other parents\n(i.e. if the child was a merge)."},"4148":{"id":"/changelog-1117","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-20","content":"The snapshot.max-new-file-size option can now handle raw integer literals,\ninterpreted as a number of bytes, where previously it could only handle string\nliterals. This means that snapshot.max-new-file-size=\"1\" and\nsnapshot.max-new-file-size=1 are now equivalent."},"4149":{"id":"/changelog-1118","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-20","content":"jj squash <path> is now a no-op if the path argument didn't match any paths\n(it used to create new commits with bumped timestamp).\n#3334"},"4150":{"id":"/changelog-1119","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"4151":{"id":"/changelog-1120","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Anton Älgmyr (@algmyr)"},"4152":{"id":"/changelog-1121","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Anton Bulakh (@necauqua)"},"4153":{"id":"/changelog-1122","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"4154":{"id":"/changelog-1123","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"4155":{"id":"/changelog-1124","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Cretezy (@Cretezy)"},"4156":{"id":"/changelog-1125","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"4157":{"id":"/changelog-1126","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Evan Mesterhazy (@emesterhazy)"},"4158":{"id":"/changelog-1127","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"4159":{"id":"/changelog-1128","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"4160":{"id":"/changelog-1129","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Noah Mayr (@noahmayr)"},"4161":{"id":"/changelog-1130","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Jeremy O'Brien (@neutralinsomniac)"},"4162":{"id":"/changelog-1131","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Jonathan Lorimer (@JonathanLorimer)"},"4163":{"id":"/changelog-1132","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"4164":{"id":"/changelog-1133","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Poliorcetics (@poliorcetics)"},"4165":{"id":"/changelog-1134","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Rowan Walsh (@rowan-walsh)"},"4166":{"id":"/changelog-1135","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Scott Olson (@solson)"},"4167":{"id":"/changelog-1136","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Théo Daron (@tdaron)"},"4168":{"id":"/changelog-1137","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-17","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"4169":{"id":"/changelog-1138","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-17","content":"jj move was deprecated in favor of jj squash."},"4170":{"id":"/changelog-1139","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-18","content":"The git_head template keyword now returns an optional value instead of a\nlist of 0 or 1 element."},"4171":{"id":"/changelog-1140","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-18","content":"The jj sparse set --edit/--reset flags were split up into jj sparse\nedit/reset subcommands respectively."},"4172":{"id":"/changelog-1141","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-18","content":"The jj sparse subcommands now parse and print patterns as workspace-relative\npaths."},"4173":{"id":"/changelog-1142","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-18","content":"The jj log command no longer uses the default revset when a path is\nspecified."},"4174":{"id":"/changelog-1143","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"Config now supports rgb hex colors (in the form #rrggbb) wherever existing\ncolor names are supported."},"4175":{"id":"/changelog-1144","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"ui.default-command now accepts multiple string arguments, for more complex\ndefault jj commands."},"4176":{"id":"/changelog-1145","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"Graph node symbols are now configurable via templates"},"4177":{"id":"/changelog-1146","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"templates.log_node"},"4178":{"id":"/changelog-1147","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"templates.op_log_node"},"4179":{"id":"/changelog-1148","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj log now includes synthetic nodes in the graph where some revisions were\nelided."},"4180":{"id":"/changelog-1149","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj squash now accepts --from and --into (also aliased as --to) if -r\nis not specified. It can now be used for all use cases where jj move could\npreviously be used. The --from argument accepts a revset that resolves to\nmore than one revision."},"4181":{"id":"/changelog-1150","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"Commit templates now support immutable keyword."},"4182":{"id":"/changelog-1151","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"New template function coalesce(content, ..) is added."},"4183":{"id":"/changelog-1152","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"Timestamps are now shown in local timezone and without milliseconds and\ntimezone offset by default."},"4184":{"id":"/changelog-1153","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj git push now prints messages from the remote."},"4185":{"id":"/changelog-1154","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj branch list now supports a --conflicted/-c option to show only\nconflicted branches."},"4186":{"id":"/changelog-1155","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj duplicate and jj abandon can now take more than a single -r argument,\nfor consistency with other commands."},"4187":{"id":"/changelog-1156","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj branch list now allows combining -r REVISIONS/NAMES and -a options."},"4188":{"id":"/changelog-1157","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"--all is now named --all-remotes for jj branch list"},"4189":{"id":"/changelog-1158","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"There is a new global --quiet flag to silence commands' non-primary output."},"4190":{"id":"/changelog-1159","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"jj split now supports a --siblings/-s option that splits the target\nrevision into siblings with the same parents and children."},"4191":{"id":"/changelog-1160","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-18","content":"New function working_copies() for revsets to show the working copy commits\nof all workspaces."},"4192":{"id":"/changelog-1161","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-21","content":"None."},"4193":{"id":"/changelog-1162","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"4194":{"id":"/changelog-1163","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Aleksey Kuznetsov (@zummenix)"},"4195":{"id":"/changelog-1164","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Anton Älgmyr (@algmyr)"},"4196":{"id":"/changelog-1165","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"4197":{"id":"/changelog-1166","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"4198":{"id":"/changelog-1167","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Chris Krycho (@chriskrycho)"},"4199":{"id":"/changelog-1168","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Christoph Koehler (@ckoehler)"},"4200":{"id":"/changelog-1169","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"4201":{"id":"/changelog-1170","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Evan Mesterhazy (@emesterhazy)"},"4202":{"id":"/changelog-1171","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"4203":{"id":"/changelog-1172","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Khionu Sybiern (@khionu)"},"4204":{"id":"/changelog-1173","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"4205":{"id":"/changelog-1174","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Matthew Davidson (@KingMob)"},"4206":{"id":"/changelog-1175","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"mrstanwell (@mrstanwell)"},"4207":{"id":"/changelog-1176","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Noah Mayr (@noahmayr)"},"4208":{"id":"/changelog-1177","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Patric Stout (@TrueBrain)"},"4209":{"id":"/changelog-1178","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Poliorcetics (@poliorcetics)"},"4210":{"id":"/changelog-1179","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Simon Wollwage (@Kintaro)"},"4211":{"id":"/changelog-1180","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Steve Klabnik (@steveklabnik)"},"4212":{"id":"/changelog-1181","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Tom Ward (@tomafro)"},"4213":{"id":"/changelog-1182","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"TrashCan (@TrashCan69420)"},"4214":{"id":"/changelog-1183","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-18","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"4215":{"id":"/changelog-1184","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#0151---2024-03-06","content":"No code changes (fixing Rust Cargo.toml stuff)."},"4216":{"id":"/changelog-1185","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"The minimum supported Rust version (MSRV) is now 1.76.0."},"4217":{"id":"/changelog-1186","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"The on-disk index format changed. New index files will be created\nautomatically, but it can fail if the repository is colocated and predates\nGit GC issues #815. If\nreindexing failed, you'll need to clean up corrupted operation history by\njj op abandon ..<bad operation ID>."},"4218":{"id":"/changelog-1187","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"Dropped support for the \"legacy\" graph-drawing style. Use \"ascii\" for a very\nsimilar result."},"4219":{"id":"/changelog-1188","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"The default log output no longer lists all tagged heads. Set revsets.log =\n\"@ | ancestors(immutable_heads().., 2) | heads(immutable_heads())\" to restore\nthe old behavior."},"4220":{"id":"/changelog-1189","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"Dropped support for the deprecated : revset operator. Use :: instead."},"4221":{"id":"/changelog-1190","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-19","content":"jj rebase --skip-empty no longer abandons commits that were already empty\nbefore the rebase."},"4222":{"id":"/changelog-1191","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Partial support for commit signing. Currently you can configure jj to \"keep\"\ncommit signatures by making new ones for rewritten commits, and to sign new\ncommits when they are created."},"4223":{"id":"/changelog-1192","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"This comes with out-of-the-box support for the following backends:"},"4224":{"id":"/changelog-1193","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"GnuPG"},"4225":{"id":"/changelog-1194","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"SSH"},"4226":{"id":"/changelog-1195","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Signature verification and an explicit sign command will hopefully come soon."},"4227":{"id":"/changelog-1196","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Templates now support logical operators: ||, &&, !"},"4228":{"id":"/changelog-1197","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Templates now support the self keyword, which is the current commit in jj\nlog/obslog templates."},"4229":{"id":"/changelog-1198","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj show now accepts -T/--template option to render its output using\ntemplate"},"4230":{"id":"/changelog-1199","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj config list now accepts -T/--template option."},"4231":{"id":"/changelog-1200","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj git fetch now accepts -b as a shorthand for --branch, making it more\nconsistent with other commands that accept a branch"},"4232":{"id":"/changelog-1201","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"In the templating language, Timestamps now have a .local() method for\nconverting to the local timezone."},"4233":{"id":"/changelog-1202","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj next/prev now infer --edit when you're already editing a non-head\ncommit (a commit with children)."},"4234":{"id":"/changelog-1203","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"A new built-in pager named :builtin is available on all platforms,\nimplemented with minus"},"4235":{"id":"/changelog-1204","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Set config ui.log-synthetic-elided-nodes = true to make jj log include\nsynthetic nodes in the graph where some revisions were elided\n(#1252,\n#2971). This may become the\ndefault depending on feedback."},"4236":{"id":"/changelog-1205","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"When creating a new workspace, the sparse patterns are now copied over from\nthe current workspace."},"4237":{"id":"/changelog-1206","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj git init --colocate can now import an existing Git repository. This is\nequivalent to jj git init --git-repo=.."},"4238":{"id":"/changelog-1207","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj git fetch now automatically prints new remote branches and tags by\ndefault."},"4239":{"id":"/changelog-1208","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"--verbose/-v is now --debug (no short option since it's not intended to be\nused often)"},"4240":{"id":"/changelog-1209","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj move --from/--to can now be abbreviated to jj move -f/-t"},"4241":{"id":"/changelog-1210","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj commit/diffedit/move/resolve/split/squash/unsquash now accept\n--tool=<NAME> option to override the default.\n#2575"},"4242":{"id":"/changelog-1211","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Added completions for Nushell to jj util completion"},"4243":{"id":"/changelog-1212","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj branch list now supports a --tracked/-t option which can be used to\nshow tracked branches only. Omits local Git-tracking branches by default."},"4244":{"id":"/changelog-1213","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"Commands producing diffs now accept a --context flag for the number of\nlines of context to show."},"4245":{"id":"/changelog-1214","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-19","content":"jj commands with the -T/--template option now provide a hint containing\ndefined template names when no argument is given, assisting the user in making\na selection."},"4246":{"id":"/changelog-1215","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-22","content":"On Windows, symlinks in the repo are now supported when Developer Mode is\nenabled.\nWhen symlink support is unavailable, they will be materialized as regular\nfiles in the\nworking copy (instead of resulting in a crash).\n#2"},"4247":{"id":"/changelog-1216","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-22","content":"On Windows, the :builtin pager is now used by default, rather than being\ndisabled entirely."},"4248":{"id":"/changelog-1217","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-22","content":"Auto-rebase now preserves the shape of history even for merge commits where\none parent is an ancestor of another.\n#2600"},"4249":{"id":"/changelog-1218","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Thanks to the people who made this release happen!"},"4250":{"id":"/changelog-1219","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Aleksey Kuznetsov (@zummenix)"},"4251":{"id":"/changelog-1220","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Anton Bulakh (@necauqua)"},"4252":{"id":"/changelog-1221","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Anton Älgmyr (@algmyr)"},"4253":{"id":"/changelog-1222","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Austin Seipp (@thoughtpolice)"},"4254":{"id":"/changelog-1223","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Benjamin Brittain (@benbrittain)"},"4255":{"id":"/changelog-1224","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Benjamin Tan (@bnjmnt4n)"},"4256":{"id":"/changelog-1225","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Daehyeok Mun (@daehyeok)"},"4257":{"id":"/changelog-1226","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Daniel Ploch (@torquestomp)"},"4258":{"id":"/changelog-1227","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Evan Mesterhazy (@emesterhazy)"},"4259":{"id":"/changelog-1228","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"gulbanana (@gulbanana)"},"4260":{"id":"/changelog-1229","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Ilya Grigoriev (@ilyagr)"},"4261":{"id":"/changelog-1230","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Jonathan Tan (@jonathantanmy)"},"4262":{"id":"/changelog-1231","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Julien Vincent (@julienvincent)"},"4263":{"id":"/changelog-1232","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"jyn (@jyn514)"},"4264":{"id":"/changelog-1233","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Martin von Zweigbergk (@martinvonz)"},"4265":{"id":"/changelog-1234","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Paulo Coelho (@prscoelho)"},"4266":{"id":"/changelog-1235","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Philip Metzger (@PhilipMetzger)"},"4267":{"id":"/changelog-1236","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Poliorcetics (@poliorcetics)"},"4268":{"id":"/changelog-1237","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Stephen Jennings (@jennings)"},"4269":{"id":"/changelog-1238","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Vladimir (@0xdeafbeef)"},"4270":{"id":"/changelog-1239","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#contributors-19","content":"Yuya Nishihara (@yuja)"},"4271":{"id":"/changelog-1240","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"jj checkout and jj merge are both deprecated; use jj new instead to\nreplace both of these commands in all instances."},"4272":{"id":"/changelog-1241","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"Rationale: jj checkout and jj merge both implement identical\nfunctionality, which is a subset of jj new. checkout creates a new working\ncopy commit on top of a single specified revision, i.e. with one parent.\nmerge creates a new working copy commit on top of at least two specified\nrevisions, i.e. with two or more parents."},"4273":{"id":"/changelog-1242","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"The only difference between these commands and jj new, which also creates\na new working copy commit, is that new can create a working copy commit on\ntop of any arbitrary number of revisions, so it can handle both the previous\ncases at once. The only actual difference between these three commands is the\ncommand syntax and their name. These names were chosen to be familiar to users\nof other version control systems, but we instead encourage all users to adopt\njj new instead; it is more general and easier to remember than both of\nthese."},"4274":{"id":"/changelog-1243","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"jj checkout and jj merge will no longer be shown as part of jj help, but\nwill still function for now, emitting a warning about their deprecation."},"4275":{"id":"/changelog-1244","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"Deadline: jj checkout and jj merge will be deleted and are expected\nbecome a hard error later in 2024."},"4276":{"id":"/changelog-1245","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"jj init --git and jj init --git-repo are now deprecated and will be\nremoved\nin the near future."},"4277":{"id":"/changelog-1246","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#deprecations-18","content":"Use jj git init instead."},"4278":{"id":"/changelog-1247","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-20","content":"(Minor) Diff summaries (e.g. jj diff -s) now use D for \"Deleted\" instead\nof R for \"Removed\". @joyously pointed out that R could also mean\n\"Renamed\"."},"4279":{"id":"/changelog-1248","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-20","content":"jj util completion now takes the shell as a positional argument, not a flag.\nthe previous behavior is deprecated, but supported for now. it will be removed\nin the future."},"4280":{"id":"/changelog-1249","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#breaking-changes-20","content":"jj rebase now preserves the shape of history even for merge commits where\none parent is an ancestor of another. You can follow the jj rebase by\njj rebase -s <merge commit> -d <single parent> if you want to linearize the\nhistory."},"4281":{"id":"/changelog-1250","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj util completion now supports powershell and elvish."},"4282":{"id":"/changelog-1251","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"Official binaries for macOS running on Apple Silicon (aarch64-apple-darwin)\nare now available, alongside the existing macOS x86 binaries."},"4283":{"id":"/changelog-1252","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"New jj op abandon command is added to clean up the operation history. Git\nrefs and commit objects can be further compacted by jj util gc."},"4284":{"id":"/changelog-1253","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj util gc now removes unreachable operation, view, and Git objects."},"4285":{"id":"/changelog-1254","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj branch rename will now warn if the renamed branch has a remote branch,\nsince\nthose will have to be manually renamed outside of jj."},"4286":{"id":"/changelog-1255","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj git push gained a --tracked option, to push all the tracked branches."},"4287":{"id":"/changelog-1256","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"There's now a virtual root operation, similar to the virtual root\ncommit. It appears at the end of jj op log."},"4288":{"id":"/changelog-1257","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj config list gained a --include-overridden option to allow\nprinting overridden config values."},"4289":{"id":"/changelog-1258","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj config list now accepts --user or --repo option to specify\nconfig origin."},"4290":{"id":"/changelog-1259","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"New jj config path command to print the config file path without launching\nan editor."},"4291":{"id":"/changelog-1260","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj tag list command prints imported git tags."},"4292":{"id":"/changelog-1261","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj next and jj prev now prompt in the event of the next/previous commit\nbeing ambiguous, instead of failing outright."},"4293":{"id":"/changelog-1262","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj resolve now displays the file being resolved."},"4294":{"id":"/changelog-1263","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj workspace root was aliased to jj root, for ease of discoverability"},"4295":{"id":"/changelog-1264","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj diff no longer shows the contents of binary files."},"4296":{"id":"/changelog-1265","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"jj git now has an init command that initializes a git backed repo."},"4297":{"id":"/changelog-1266","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#new-features-20","content":"New template function surround(prefix, suffix, content) is added."},"4298":{"id":"/changelog-1267","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/changelog#fixed-bugs-23","content":"Fixed snapshots of symlinks in gitignore-d directory.\n#2878"},"4299":{"id":"/changelog-1268","page_id":"/changelog","tags":[],"type":"tex