s,\nyou can duplicate one of the commits to generate a new change ID, then abandon\nthe original:"],[558,"If you want to know the internals of bookmark tracking, consult the\nDesign Doc."],[918,"If you want to preserve some of the changes you made, you can do jj bookmark\n    set my-changes -r gh-pages BEFORE running the above commands."],[2065,"If you want to see the config variable origin (type and path) when you do jj config list\nyou can add this to your config:"],[2076,"If you want to see the full description when you do jj log you can add this to\nyour config:"],[1743,"If you'd like to install a prerelease version, you'll need to use one of the\noptions below."],[2119,"If you'd like to pass the output through a formatter e.g.\ndiff-so-fancy before piping it\nthrough a pager you must do it using a subshell as, unlike git or hg, the\ncommand will be executed directly. For example:"],[65,"If you're familiar with Git, you might expect the current bookmark to move forward\nwhen you commit. However, Jujutsu does not have a concept of a \"current bookmark\"."],[243,"If you're not sure what to say, we hired the cheapest marketing team we could\nfind to design a list of Pre-Approved Endorsements in their laboratory. Just\ncopy and paste these right into a text box! Shilling for an open source project\nhas never been easier than this."],[1749,"If you're on NixOS you can install a released version of jj using the\nnixpkgs jujutsu package."],[1707,"If you're wondering why we prefer clean commits in this project, see\ne.g. this blog post"],[848,"If your employer pays anyone (not necessarily you) to contribute to Jujutsu,\nplease make sure your GitHub username is recorded.\nTo avoid conflicts of interest, please don't merge a PR that has only been\napproved by someone from the same organization. Similarly, as a reviewer, there\nis no need to approve your coworkers' PRs, since the author should await an\napproval from someone else anyway. It is of course still appreciated if