mutable_heads(): Resolves to\npresent(trunk()) | tags() | untracked_remote_bookmarks() by default. It is\nactually defined as builtin_immutable_heads(), and can be overridden as\nrequired. See here for details."],[2581,"immutable(): The set of commits that jj treats as immutable. This is\nequivalent to ::(immutable_heads() | root()). It is not recommended to redefine\nthis alias. Note that modifying this will not change whether a commit is immutable.\nTo do that, edit immutable_heads()."],[1188,"Implement blame algorithm and test it"],[1192,"Implement CLI for recording copies and for resolving conflicts in copies"],[1186,"Implement diff algorithm and test it"],[1189,"Implement file-following log algorithm and test it"],[1187,"Implement merge algorithm and test it"],[1191,"Implement support for copy-tracking in the Git backend. This may involve\nbackfilling, possibly lazily. Or it may involve new abstractions in the\ncommit backend trait."],[1185,"Implement support for copy-tracking in the test backend"],[1086,"Implementation plan"],[4489,"Implicit concatenation of template expressions has been disabled. Use\n++ operator, concat(), or separate() function instead.\nExample: description ++ \"\\n\""],[1521,"Import changes only for remotes[remote].branches[glob] (see below)"],[1553,"Import, track, and merge per git.auto_local_branch config."],[1556,"Import, track, and merge per git.auto_local_branch config."],[1477,"Import/export data flow"],[3648,"Improved Git push/fetch compatibility by spawning an external git process.\nThis can be enabled by the git.subprocess=true config knob, and will be the\ndefault in a future release."],[3732,"Improvements to configuration management, including support for conditional\nvariables in config files."],[1686,"In a colocated repository, every jj command will automatically synchronize\nJujutsu's view of the repo with Git's view. For example, jj commit updates the\nHEAD of the Git repository, enabling an incremental migration."],[1687,"In a Jujutsu repository, the workflow is simplified. If there's no need for\nexplicitly named bookmarks, you can just generate one for a change. As Jujutsu is\nable to create a bookmark for a revision."],[1282,"In a superproject commit, submodule information is captured in two places:"],[195,"In addition to helping with the problem of unknown backends, having an RPC API\nshould make it easier for tools like VS Code that are not written in Rust. The\nRPC API will probably be at a higher abstraction level than the Rust API."],[2906,"In addition to that, you can insert arbitrary labels by label(label, content)\nfunction."],[856,"In addition to the Rust Book and the other\nexcellent resources at https://www.rust-lang.org/learn, we recommend the\n\"Comprehensive Rust\" mini-course\nfor an overview, especially if you are familiar with C++."],[471,"In colocated repos with a very large number of branches or other refs, jj\ncommands can get noticeably slower because of the automatic jj git import\nexecuted on each command. This can be mitigated by occasionally running jj util\ngc to speed up the import (that command includes packing the Git refs)."],[4539,"In colocated repos, a bug causing conflicts when undoing branch moves (#922)\nhas been fixed. Some surprising behaviors related to undoing jj git push or\njj git fetch remain."],[3547,"In colocated repos, any files that jj considers added in the working copy will\nnow show up in git diff (as if you had run git add --intent-to-add on\nthem)."],[3513,"In colocated repos, newly-created files will now appear in git diff."],[3659,"In colocated repos, the Git index now contains the changes from all parents\nof the working copy instead of just the first parent (HEAD). 2-sided\nconflicts from the merged parents are now added to the Git index as conflicts\nas well."],[2030,"In color-words and git diffs, word-level hunks are rendered with underline. You\ncan override the default style with the following keys:"],[2031,"In color-words diffs, changed words are displayed inline by default. Because\nit's difficult to read a diff line with many removed/added words, there's a\nthreshold to switch to traditional separate-line format. You can also change\nthe default number of lines of context shown."],[4046,"In color-words diffs, hunks are now highlighted with underline. See diff\ncolors and styles for customization."],[4594,"In content that goes to the terminal, the ANSI escape byte (0x1b) is replaced\nby a \"␛\" character. That prevents them from interfering with the ANSI escapes\njj itself writes."],[2044,"In git diffs you can change the default number of lines of context shown."],[3974,"In git diffs, word-level hunks are now highlighted with underline. See diff\ncolors and styles for customization."],[3664,"In jj config list template, value is now typed as ConfigValue, not as\nString serialized in TOML syntax."],[2649,"In jj log templates, all 0-argument methods of the Commit\ntype are available as keywords. For example, commit_id is\nequivalent to self.commit_id()."],[2650,"In jj op log templates, all 0-argument methods of the Operation\ntype are available as keywords. For example,\ncurrent_operation is equivalent to self.current_operation()."],[2245,"In large repositories, it may be beneficial to use a \"filesystem monitor\" to\ntrack changes to the working copy. This allows jj to take working copy\nsnapshots without having to rescan the entire working copy."],[198,"In order to reduce latency, there is a local daemon process that caches reads\nand writes. It also prefetches of objects it thinks the client might ask for\nnext. In also helps with write latency by optimistically answering write\nrequests (it therefore needs to know the server's hashing scheme so it can\nreturn the right IDs)."],[4095,"In other words, previously branches that moved sideways or backward were\npushed similarly to Git's git push --force; now they have protections\nsimilar to git push --force-with-lease (though not identical to it, to match\nthe behavior of jj git fetch). Note also that because of the way jj git\nfetch works, jj does not suffer from the same problems as Git's git push\n--force-with-lease in situations when git fetch is run in the background."],[1454,"In particular, the path rules for sparse patterns will always be repo paths,\nnot working copy paths. Thus, if the working copy wants to track \"foo\" and\nrename it to \"subdir/bar\", they must jj sparse set --add foo and\njj map set --from foo --to bar. In other words, the mapping operation can\nbe thought of as always after the sparse operation."],[610,"In practice, conflicts are usually 2-sided, meaning that there's only 2\nconflicting changes being merged together at a time, but Jujutsu supports\nconflicts with arbitrarily many sides, which can happen when merging 3 or more\ncommits at once. In that case, you would see a single snapshot section and\nmultiple diff sections."],[4023,"In revset aliases, top-level kind:pattern expression is now parsed as\nmodifier. Surround with parentheses if it should be parsed as string/file\npattern."],[3301,"In revsets, symbol expressions (such as change ID prefix) no longer resolve to\nmultiple revisions, and error out if resolved to more than one revisions. Use\nchange_id(prefix) or bookmarks(exact:name) to query divergent changes or\nconflicted bookmarks. Commands like jj rebase no longer require all: to\nspecify multiple destination revisions."],[4428,"In revsets, the working-copy or remote symbols (such as @, workspace_id@,\nand branch@remote) can no longer be quoted as a unit. If a workspace or\nbranch name contains whitespace, quote the name like \"branch name\"@remote.\nAlso, these symbols will not be resolved as revset aliases or function\nparameters. For example, author(foo@) is now an error, and the revset alias\n'revset-aliases.foo@' = '@' will be failed to parse."],[4771,"In short, Maintainers are the outwardly visible stewards of the project."],[1056,"In some cases, implementation may also involve nomination of individuals to a\ngroup or committee. When this is necessary, expect the policy being proposed to\ndescribe how these individuals will be nominated, both initially and moving into\nthe future."],[2068,"In some situations the default graph can be hard to read, for example when working with big merges.\nTo improve this behavior you can configure which revset in the jj log graph is displayed on\nthe left instead of @."],[3403,"In templates, bookmark/tag/remote names are now formatted in revset symbol\nnotation. The type of bookmark.remote() is changed to Option<_>.\nbookmark.remote() == \"foo\" still works, but bookmark.remote().<method>()\nmight need if(bookmark.remote(), ..) to suppress error."],[654,"In the context of jj, the work \"branch\" usually refers to an anonymous\nbranch or, less formally, a branch of the commit \"tree\"\n(which is itself an informal way to refer to the commit graph, parts of which\nmight resemble a tree even when it's not mathematically a tree)."],[1833,"In the diff editor, use the arrow keys and spacebar to select all lines but the\nlast. Press 'c' to save the changes and close it. You can now inspect the\nrewritten commit with jj diff -r @- again, and you should see your deletion of\nthe last line. Unlike jj squash -i, which left the content state of the commit\nunchanged, jj diffedit (typically) results in a different state, which means\nthat descendant commits may have conflicts."],[4799,"In the event that a decision is reached before the proposed timeline, said\nproposal can move on and be accepted immediately. In the event no consensus is\nreached, a proposal may be re-submitted later on."],[1518,"In the following sections, a merge is expressed as adds - removes.\nIn particular, a merge of local and remote targets is\n[local, remote] - [known_remote]."],[4232,"In the templating language, Timestamps now have a .local() method for\nconverting to the local timezone."],[2194,"In the user configuration, define a disabled tool for running rustfmt:"],[1287,"In the working tree, Git notices the presence of a submodule by the .git entry\n(signifying the root of a Git repository working tree). This is either the\nsubmodule's actual Git directory (an \"old-form\" submodule), or a .git file\npointing to <superproject-git-directory>/modules/<submodule-name>. The latter\nis sometimes called the \"absorbed form\", and is Git's preferred mode of\noperation."],[2455,"In this documentation, optional arguments are indicated with square\nbrackets like [arg]. Some arguments also have an optional label which can\nbe used to specify that argument without specifying all previous arguments."],[1681,"In this example we're letting Jujutsu auto-create a bookmark."],[129,"In this example, the version of the change when we were actually done with\nfeature A is when we edited the file to say \"Done with feature A\". This state\nwas saved in the commit with ID b80 (the second one in the list). The\nfollowing edit (commit 31a) belongs in a new change."],[1682,"In this example, we create a bookmark named bar and then push it to the remote."],[1167,"In this scenario, the regular 3-way merge of the trees without considering copy\ninfo results in a tree without conflicts. However, the user might reasonably\nexpect to have to choose between the bar and baz names. Here's what Git says\nin this scenario:"],[1991,"In TOML, anything under a heading can be dotted instead. For example,\nuser.name = \"YOUR NAME\" is equivalent to:"],[1090,"Include copy info in the FileId (Mercurial-like model)"],[951,"incognito124"],[91,"Indeed, every jj command updates the current \"working-copy\" revision, marked\nwith @ in jj log. You can notice this by how the commit ID of the\nworking copy revision changes when it's updated. Note that, unless you move to\nanother revision (with jj new or jj edit, for example), the change ID will\nnot change."],[2665,"indent(prefix: Template, content: Template) -> Template: Indent\nnon-empty lines by the given prefix."],[4320,"Information about new and resolved conflicts is now printed by every command."],[4388,"Infra (@1011X)"],[1483,"init/clone"],[1729,"Initial configuration"],[3844,"Initial support for shallow Git repositories has been implemented. However,\ndeepening the history of a shallow repository is not yet supported."],[4525,"Initial support for the Watchman filesystem monitor. Set\ncore.fsmonitor = \"watchman\" in your repo to enable."],[1337,"Initial Version, 10.12.2022 (view full history here)"],[1774,"Insert this line in your $PROFILE file\n(usually $HOME\\Documents\\PowerShell\\Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1):"],[2288,"Install Even Better TOML"],[2296,"Install lsp-mode and toml-mode"],[2292,"Install taplo"],[923,"Install the protoc compiler. This usually means either apt-get install\nprotobuf-compiler or downloading an official release. The\nprost library docs have additional advice."],[2294,"Install TOML plugin"],[831,"Install uv"],[913,"Install uv as explained in Previewing the HTML\ndocumentation, and run the same sh script\nthat is used in GitHub CI (details below):"],[1714,"Installation"],[174,"Installation and setup"],[1713,"Installation and setup"],[761,"Instances of abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behavior may be\nreported to the community leaders responsible for enforcement at\ntwo or more of jaraco@jaraco.com, icorbrey@gmail.com, me@waleedkhan.name, and opensource@google.com.\nAll complaints will be reviewed and investigated promptly and fairly."],[2216,"Instead of signing all commits during creation when signing.behavior is\nset to own, the git.sign-on-push configuration can be used to sign\ncommits only upon running jj git push. All mutable unsigned commits\nbeing pushed will be signed prior to pushing. This might be preferred if the\nsigning backend requires user interaction or is slow, so that signing is\nperformed in a single batch operation."],[480,"Instead of the echo -n ... line, use:\nSet-Content -Path .jj/repo/store/git_target -Value ../../../.git -NoNewLine"],[2618,"Integer type"],[1333,"Integrating with other commands"],[1406,"Integration options for virtual filesystems, which allow them to cache the\nneeded working copies."],[385,"Interactively edit the diff in a given change"],[376,"Interactively move part of the diff in an arbitrary change to another arbitrary change"],[370,"Interactively move part of the diff in the current change into the parent change"],[382,"Interactively split an arbitrary change in two"],[379,"Interactively split the changes in the working copy in two"],[3805,"interdiff"],[1168,"Interestingly, Git seems to represent this state by using index states that\nwould not normally end up in the index as a result of conflicts."],[87,"Interleaving git and jj commands may create confusing bookmark conflicts\nor divergent changes."],[469,"Interleaving jj and git commands increases the chance of confusing branch\nconflicts or conflicted (AKA divergent) change\nids. These never lose data, but can be\nannoying."],[1255,"Intro to Git Submodules"],[1317,"Introducing JJ run"],[489,"Introduction"],[515,"Introduction"],[538,"Introduction"],[590,"Introduction"],[691,"Introduction"],[706,"Introduction"],[1001,"Introduction"],[2979,"Introduction"],[3001,"Introduction"],[682,"Intuitively, visible commits are the \"latest versions\" of a revision with a\ngiven change id. A commit that's abandoned or\nrewritten stops being visible and is labeled as \"hidden\". Such\ncommits are no longer accessible using a change id, but they are still\naccessible by their commit id."],[3891,"Invalid ui.graph.style configuration is now an error."],[49,"Is there something like git rebase --interactive or hg histedit?"],[70,"Is your commit visible with jj log -r 'all()'?"],[3291,"Isaac Corbrey (@icorbrey)"],[3435,"Isaac Corbrey (@icorbrey)"],[4389,"Isabella Basso (@isinyaaa)"],[4551,"Isabella Basso (@isinyaaa)"],[783,"Issues addressed (optional)"],[998,"It can still be useful to add a test case or two to check that the lower-level\nfunctionality is correctly hooked up in the CLI. For example, the end-to-end\ntests for jj log don't need to test that all kinds of revsets are evaluated\ncorrectly (we have tests in jj-lib for that), but they should check that the\n-r flag is respected."],[466,"It is allowed to mix jj and git commands in such a repo in any order.\nHowever, it may be easier to keep track of what is going on if you mostly use\nread-only git commands and use jj to make changes to the repo. One reason\nfor this (see below for more) is that jj commands will usually put the git\nrepo in a \"detached HEAD\" state, since in jj there is not concept of a\n\"currently tracked branch\". Before doing mutating Git commands, you may need to\ntell Git what the current branch should be with a git switch command."],[1708,"It is common to use several remotes when contributing to a shared repository.\nFor example, \"upstream\" can designate the remote where the changes will be\nmerged through a pull-request while \"origin\" is your private fork of the\nproject."],[1874,"It is made the working copy. jj edit REV will make REV and all its\nancestors visible if it wasn't already."],[4532,"It is no longer allowed to create branches at the root commit."],[4605,"It is now possible to change the author format of jj log with the\nformat_short_signature() template alias. For details, see\nthe documentation."],[4536,"It is now possible to jj branch forget deleted branches.\n#1537"],[4527,"It is now possible to modify either side of a modify/delete conflict (any\nchange used to be considered a resolution)."],[4446,"It is now possible to set a default description using the new\nui.default-description option, to use when describing changes with an empty\ndescription."],[4650,"It is now possible to specify configuration options on the command line\nwith the new --config-toml global option."],[102,"It is often sufficient to use some form of jj rebase with -A/-B. For\nexample, if you have a linear chain of revisions A through C and want to\nmove C before B, use jj rebase -r C -B B. See jj help rebase for more\nexamples."],[2098,"It is possible the default will change to :builtin for all platforms in the\nfuture."],[2995,"It is possible to load the repo at a particular operation with\njj --at-operation=<operation ID> <command>. If the command is mutational, that\nwill result in a fork in the operation log. That works exactly the same as if\nany later operations had not existed when the command started. In other words,\nrunning commands on a repo loaded at an earlier operation works the same way as\nif the operations had been concurrent. This can be useful for simulating\ndivergent operations."],[1379,"It may be useful to execute commands in topological order. For example,\ncommands with costs proportional to incremental changes, like build systems.\nThere may also be other relevant heuristics, but topological order is an easy\nand effective way to start."],[1162,"It seems clear that baz's copy graph should inherit from both foo and bar,\nproducing a merge in copy graph. The trees would look like this:"],[1387,"It will be useful to constrain the execution to prevent resource exhaustion.\nRelevant resources could include:"],[1382,"It will be useful to have multiple strategies to deal with failures on a single\nor multiple revisions. The reason for these strategies is to allow customized\nconflict handling. These strategies then can be exposed in the ui with a\nmatching option."],[1194,"It's hard to make this model scale to very large repos. For example, let's say\nyou're rebasing your local commit to a new upstream commit that's 1 million\ncommits ahead. We would then want to find if any of the files in your local\ncommit has been copied upstream. That's very expensive to do by comparing the\nold and the new base trees. However, since the query APIs defined above take\ncommits (not trees) as input, we allow the backend to take the history into\naccount when calculating the copies. A backend can then create an index based\non the input files (in your local commit) and find if it's been copied without\ncomparing the full trees."],[1017,"It's intended to meet community members where they are - on GitHub and on\nDiscord, where all development occurs and most support and technical\ndiscussion occurs."],[4432,"It's no longer allowed to create a Git remote named \"git\". Use jj git remote\nrename to rename the existing remote.\n#1690"],[4367,"It's not allowed to push branches if non-tracking remote branches of the same\nname exist."],[1057,"It's possible (but unlikely) that during implementation, some obstacle will\narise that means the policy doesn't actually work. If this does happen, expect\nthe working group to be transparent with the community about the situation. We\nmay reuse some of all of this process to figure out how to move forward."],[212,"It's the easiest time I've ever had learning a tool this deeply this quickly,\nbecause of the ability to experiment and undo, instead of triple-checking\nbefore trying a new scary command."],[3731,"It's the holidays, and this release was overall pretty quiet, without many major\nchanges. Two select improvements:"],[3688,"Italic text is now supported. You can set e.g. colors.error = { fg = \"red\",\nitalic = true } in your config."],[808,"Iterate until everyone accepts the change in normal codereview fashion."],[3292,"Ivan Petkov (@ipetkov)"],[3485,"Jacob Hayes (@JacobHayes)"],[3633,"Jacob Hayes (@JacobHayes)"],[3339,"Jade Lovelace (@lf-)"],[3385,"Jade Lovelace (@lf-)"],[3340,"Jake Martin (@jake-m-commits)"],[3572,"Jakob Hellermann (@jakobhellermann)"],[3713,"Jakob Hellermann (@jakobhellermann)"],[3871,"Jakub Okoński (@farnoy)"],[4061,"James Sully (@sullyj3)"],[4410,"James Sully (@sullyj3)"],[3341,"Jan Klass (@Kissaki)"],[4349,"Jason R. Coombs (@jaraco)"],[3872,"Jcparkyn (@Jcparkyn)"],[3714,"JDSeiler (@JDSeiler)"],[4161,"Jeremy O'Brien (@neutralinsomniac)"],[4350,"Jesse Somerville (@jessesomerville)"],[2293,"JetBrains IDEs (IntelliJ, PyCharm, etc)"],[3969,"jj --at-op=@ no longer merges concurrent operations if explicitly specified."],[4681,"jj [op] undo and jj op restore used to take the operation to undo or\nrestore to as an argument to -o/--operation. It is now a positional\nargument instead (i.e. jj undo -o abc123 is now written jj undo abc123)."],[328,"jj abandon"],[3517,"jj abandon no longer supports --summary to suppress the list of abandoned\ncommits. The list won't show more than 10 commits to not clutter the console."],[3650,"jj abandon now deletes bookmarks pointing to the revisions to be abandoned.\nUse --retain-bookmarks to move bookmarks backwards. If deleted bookmarks\nwere tracking remote bookmarks, the associated bookmarks (or branches) will be\ndeleted from the remote on jj git push --all.\n#3505"],[3463,"jj absorb can now squash a deleted file if it was added by one of the\ndestination revisions."],[3740,"jj absorb now abandons the source commit if it becomes empty and has no\ndescription."],[2011,"jj also supports colors from the ANSI 256-color palette as ansi-color-<N>,\nwhere <N> is a number between 0 and 255:"],[3964,"jj backout --revision has been renamed to jj backout --revisions.\nThe short alias -r is still supported."],[3979,"jj backout can now back out multiple commits at once."],[3528,"jj backout is deprecated in favor of jj revert."],[3978,"jj backout now includes the backed out commit's subject in the new commit\nmessage."],[403,"jj bookmark create <name> -r <revision>"],[3591,"jj bookmark create, jj bookmark set and jj bookmark move onto a hidden\ncommit make it visible."],[412,"jj bookmark delete <name>"],[3592,"jj bookmark forget now untracks any corresponding remote bookmarks instead\nof forgetting them, since forgetting a remote bookmark can be unintuitive.\nThe old behavior is still available with the new --include-remotes flag."],[3847,"jj bookmark list gained a --remote REMOTE option to display bookmarks\nbelonging to a remote. This option can be combined with --tracked or\n--conflicted."],[3544,"jj bookmark list now supports --sort option. Similar to git branch --sort.\nSee jj bookmark list --help for more details."],[400,"jj bookmark list or jj b l for short"],[3543,"jj bookmark move --to/--from can now be abbreviated to jj bookmark move -t/-f"],[409,"jj bookmark move <name> --to <revision> --allow-backwards"],[406,"jj bookmark move <name> --to <revision> or jj b m <name> --to <revision> for short"],[4712,"jj branch can accept any number of branches to update, rather than just one."],[1560,"jj branch delete {name}"],[4374,"jj branch delete/forget/list, and jj git push --branch now support\nstring pattern syntax. The --glob option\nis deprecated in favor of glob: pattern."],[1500,"jj branch forget"],[1562,"jj branch forget {name}"],[3893,"jj branch has been deprecated in favor of jj bookmark."],[4321,"jj branch has gained a new rename subcommand that allows changing a branch\nname atomically. jj branch help rename for details."],[1571,"jj branch list"],[4524,"jj branch list can now be filtered by revset."],[4187,"jj branch list now allows combining -r REVISIONS/NAMES and -a options."],[4185,"jj branch list now supports a --conflicted/-c option to show only\nconflicted branches."],[4243,"jj branch list now supports a --tracked/-t option which can be used to\nshow tracked branches only. Omits local Git-tracking branches by default."],[4083,"jj branch list/tag list now accept -T/--template option. The tag list\nprints commit summary along with the tag name by default."],[4687,"jj branch now uses subcommands like jj branch create and\njj branch forget instead of options like jj branch --forget.\n#330"],[3997,"jj branch rename no longer shows a warning in colocated repos."],[4285,"jj branch rename will now warn if the renamed branch has a remote branch,\nsince\nthose will have to be manually renamed outside of jj."],[1558,"jj branch set {name}"],[4333,"jj branch set no longer creates a new branch. Use jj branch create\ninstead."],[4027,"jj branch set now creates new branch if it doesn't exist. Use jj branch\nmove to ensure that the target branch already exists.\n#3584"],[1565,"jj branch track {name}@{remote} (new command)"],[4086,"jj branch track now show conflicts if there are some."],[1569,"jj branch untrack {name}@{remote} (new command)"],[1642,"jj branch untrack {name}@git"],[2242,"jj by default resolves content conflicts by splitting text into line-level\nhunks and merge them. This can be configured to split hunks further into\nword-level hunks."],[2196,"jj can be configured to sign and verify the commits it creates using either\nGnuPG or SSH signing keys."],[3653,"jj cat is replaced by jj file show."],[4271,"jj checkout and jj merge are both deprecated; use jj new instead to\nreplace both of these commands in all instances."],[4274,"jj checkout and jj merge will no longer be shown as part of jj help, but\nwill still function for now, emitting a warning about their deprecation."],[3788,"jj checkout and the built-in alias jj co have been removed.\nIt was deprecated in 0.14.0."],[4719,"jj checkout now lets you specify a description with --message/-m."],[4445,"jj checkout/jj describe/jj commit/jj new/jj squash can take repeated\n-m/--message arguments. Each passed message will be combined into paragraphs\n(separated by a blank line)"],[3654,"jj chmod is replaced by jj file chmod."],[3743,"jj command no longer fails due to new working-copy files larger than the\nsnapshot.max-new-file-size config option. It will print a warning and large\nfiles will be left untracked."],[4245,"jj commands with the -T/--template option now provide a hint containing\ndefined template names when no argument is given, assisting the user in making\na selection."],[307,"jj commit"],[4402,"jj commit accepts an optional list of paths indicating a subset of files to\ninclude in the first commit"],[4403,"jj commit accepts the --interactive flag."],[3909,"jj commit and jj describe now accept --author option allowing to quickly change\nauthor of given commit."],[4641,"jj commit is now a separate command from jj close (which no longer\nexists). The behavior has changed slightly. It now always asks for a\ndescription, even if there already was a description set. It now also only\nworks on the working-copy commit (there's no -r argument)."],[4051,"jj commit now accepts --reset-author option to match jj describe."],[4241,"jj commit/diffedit/move/resolve/split/squash/unsquash now accept\n--tool=<NAME> option to override the default.\n#2575"],[3537,"jj config {edit,set,unset} now prompt when multiple config files are found."],[4437,"jj config edit --user and jj config set --user will now pick a default\nconfig location if no existing file is found, potentially creating parent\ndirectories."],[3737,"jj config edit --user now opens a file even if $JJ_CONFIG points to a\ndirectory. If there are multiple config files, the command will fail."],[3467,"jj config edit will now roll back to previous version if a syntax error has been introduced in the new config."],[4503,"jj config get command allows retrieving config values for use in scripting."],[4078,"jj config get/list/set now parse name argument as TOML\nkey. Quote meta characters as needed.\nExample: jj config get \"revset-aliases.'trunk()'\""],[4580,"jj config list command prints values from config and config edit opens\nthe config in an editor."],[4288,"jj config list gained a --include-overridden option to allow\nprinting overridden config values."],[4289,"jj config list now accepts --user or --repo option to specify\nconfig origin."],[4230,"jj config list now accepts -T/--template option."],[3661,"jj config list now prints inline tables { key = value, .. } literally.\nInner items of inline tables are no longer merged across configuration\nfiles."],[3736,"jj config list now prints inline tables { key = value, .. } literally.\nInner items of inline tables are no longer merged across configuration files.\nSee the table syntax\ndocumentation for\ndetails."],[4097,"jj config list now properly escapes TOML keys (#1322)."],[3260,"jj config list now supports -T'json(self) ++ \"\\n\"' serialization output."],[4077,"jj config list now uses multi-line strings and single-quoted strings in the\noutput when appropriate."],[3755,"jj config path --user no longer creates new file at the default config path."],[4457,"jj config set --user and jj config edit --user can now be used outside of\nany repository."],[4504,"jj config set command allows simple config edits like\njj config set --repo user.email \"somebody@example.com\""],[3738,"jj config set no longer accepts a bare string value that looks like a TOML\nexpression. For example, jj config set NAME '[foo]' must be quoted as jj\nconfig set NAME '\"[foo]\"'."],[4360,"jj config set now interprets the value as TOML also if it's a valid TOML\narray or table. For example, jj config set --user 'aliases.n' '[\"new\"]'"],[3554,"jj config set/--config value parsing rule is relaxed in a way that\nunquoted apostrophes are allowed.\n#5748"],[3812,"jj config unset <TABLE-NAME> no longer removes a table (such as [ui].)"],[4496,"jj debug completion, jj debug mangen and jj debug config-schema have\nbeen moved from jj debug to jj util."],[4581,"jj debug config-schema command prints out JSON schema for the jj TOML config\nfile format."],[340,"jj describe"],[343,"jj describe @-"],[3992,"jj describe can now update the description of multiple commits."],[3671,"jj describe now accepts --edit."],[3751,"jj describe now accepts a JJ: ignore-rest line that ignores everything\nbelow it, similar to a \"scissor line\" in git. When editing multiple commits,\nonly ignore until the next JJ: describe line."],[4508,"jj describe now supports --reset-author for resetting a commit's author\nto the configured user. jj describe also gained a --no-edit option to\navoid opening the editor."],[3461,"jj describe, jj commit, jj new, jj squash and jj split add the\ncommit trailers, configured in the commit_trailers template, to the commit\ndescription. Use cases include DCO Sign Off and Gerrit Change Id."],[280,"jj diff"],[286,"jj diff --from <revision>"],[289,"jj diff --from A --to B"],[1114,"jj diff --from C --to D should now show a baz->bar rename (just like\njj diff --from C --to B would). jj diff --from B --to D should show\nno renames. That's despite there being a rename in C."],[3994,"jj diff --git no longer shows the contents of binary files."],[4454,"jj diff --stat has been implemented. It shows a histogram of the changes,\nsame as git diff --stat.\nFixes #2066"],[3267,"jj diff --stat now shows the change in size to binary files."],[283,"jj diff -r <revision>"],[292,"jj diff -r A..B"],[3538,"jj diff -r now allows multiple revisions (as long as there are no gaps in\nthe revset), such as jj diff -r 'mutable()'."],[2320,"jj diff '\"Foo(1)\"' (both shell and inner quotes are required)"],[2319,"jj diff '~\"Foo Bar\"' (both shell and inner quotes are required)"],[2322,"jj diff '~glob:**/*.rs'"],[2318,"jj diff 'Foo Bar' (shell quotes are required, but inner quotes are optional)"],[4295,"jj diff no longer shows the contents of binary files."],[3364,"jj diff now accepts -T/--template option to customize summary output."],[4441,"jj diff/log now supports --tool <name> option to generate diffs by\nexternal program. For configuration, see the documentation.\n#1886"],[387,"jj diffedit -r <revision>"],[3315,"jj diffedit now accepts filesets to edit only the specified paths."],[3910,"jj diffedit, jj abandon, and jj restore now accept a --restore-descendants\nflag. When used, descendants of the edited or deleted commits will keep their original\ncontent."],[394,"jj duplicate <source> -d <destination>"],[4186,"jj duplicate and jj abandon can now take more than a single -r argument,\nfor consistency with other commands."],[4591,"jj duplicate can now duplicate 