gured to run different tools on different filesets.\nThis simplifies the use case of configuring code formatters for specific file\ntypes. See jj help fix for details."],[3322,"jj fix commands now replace $root with the workspace's root path. This is\nuseful for tools stored inside the workspace."],[3555,"jj fix could previously create new conflicts when a descendant of a fixed\nrevision was already correctly formatted."],[3901,"jj fix now allows fixing unchanged files with the --include-unchanged-files flag. This\ncan be used to more easily introduce automatic formatting changes in a new\ncommit separate from other changes."],[3593,"jj fix now always sets the working directory of invoked tools to be the\nworkspace root, instead of the working directory of the jj fix."],[3310,"jj fix now buffers the standard error stream from subprocesses and emits\nthe output from each all at once. The file name is printed before the output."],[4025,"jj fix now defaults to the broader revset -s reachable(@, mutable())\ninstead of -s @."],[4036,"jj fix now supports configuring the default revset for -s using the\nrevsets.fix config."],[2187,"jj fix provides the file content anonymously on standard input, but the name\nof the file being formatted may be important for include sorting or other output\nlike error messages. To address this, you can use the $path substitution to\nprovide the name of the file in a command argument."],[3670,"jj git {push,clone,fetch} can now spawn an external git subprocess, via\nthe git.subprocess = true config knob. This provides an alternative that,\nwhen turned on, fixes SSH bugs when interacting with Git remotes due to\nlibgit2s limitations #4979."],[1555,"jj git clone"],[258,"jj git clone <source> <destination> [--remote <remote name>]"],[3976,"jj git clone and jj git init with an existing git repository adds the\ndefault branch of the remote as repository settings for\nrevset-aliases.\"trunk()\".`"],[3845,"jj git clone now accepts a --depth <DEPTH> option, which\nallows to clone the repository with a given depth."],[3905,"jj git clone now accepts a --remote <REMOTE NAME> option, which\nallows to set a name for the remote instead of using the default\norigin."],[3275,"jj git clone now correctly fetches all tags, unless --fetch-tags is\nexplicitly specified, in which case the specified option will apply for both\nthe initial clone and subsequent fetches."],[4439,"jj git clone now supports the --colocate flag to create the git repo\nin the same directory as the jj repo."],[3980,"jj git clone some/nested/path now creates the full directory tree for\nnested destination paths if they don't exist."],[1543,"jj git export"],[1509,"jj git export copies jj's remotes view back to the Git repo. If a ref in\nthe Git repo has been updated since the last import, the ref isn't exported."],[1519,"jj git fetch"],[4455,"jj git fetch --all-remotes has been implemented. It fetches all remotes\ninstead of just the default remote"],[4369,"jj git fetch --branch now requires glob: prefix to expand * in branch\nname."],[1645,"jj git fetch --remote git"],[3911,"jj git fetch -b <remote-git-branch-name> will now warn if the branch(es)\ncan not be found in any of the specified/configured remotes."],[262,"jj git fetch [--remote <remote>]"],[4589,"jj git fetch accepts repeated --remote arguments."],[4515,"jj git fetch and jj git push will now use the single defined remote even\nif it is not named \"origin\"."],[4535,"jj git fetch can now fetch forgotten branches even if they didn't move on\nthe remote.\n#1714\n#1771"],[4534,"jj git fetch in a colocated repo now abandons branches deleted on the\nremote, just like in a non-colocated repo.\n#864"],[4319,"jj git fetch no longer imports new remote branches as local branches. Set\ngit.auto-local-branch = true to restore the old behavior."],[3325,"jj git fetch no longer shows NaN% progress when connecting to slow remotes.\n#7155"],[4231,"jj git fetch now accepts -b as a shorthand for --branch, making