ence over origin if both exist."],[4296,"jj git now has an init command that initializes a git backed repo."],[1534,"jj git push"],[266,"jj git push --all [--remote <remote>]"],[67,"jj git push --all pushes all bookmarks, not all revisions. You have two\noptions:"],[270,"jj git push --bookmark <bookmark name> [--remote <remote>]"],[2236,"jj git push --change generates bookmark names with a prefix of \"push-\" by\ndefault. You can pick a different prefix and formatting by setting the\ntemplates.git_push_bookmark template. For example:"],[4499,"jj git push --deleted will remove all locally deleted branches from the\nremote."],[1648,"jj git push --remote git"],[4047,"jj git push -c <arg> can now accept revsets that resolve to multiple\nrevisions. This means that jj git push -c xyz -c abc is now equivalent to\njj git push -c 'all:(xyz | abc)'."],[3452,"jj git push -c/--change no longer moves existing local bookmarks."],[2235,"jj git push does not push newly-created bookmarks by default.\nIf you do not want to specify --allow-new every time you have created a new\nbookmark, you may want to allow new bookmarks to be pushed by default:"],[4709,"jj git push gained a --change <revision> argument. When that's used, it\nwill create a branch named after the revision's change ID, so you don't have\nto create a branch yourself. By default, the branch name will start with\npush-, but this can be overridden by the push.branch-prefix config\nsetting."],[4286,"jj git push gained a --tracked option, to push all the tracked branches."],[4690,"jj git push no longer aborts if you attempt to push an open commit (but it\nnow aborts if a commit does not have a description)."],[3790,"jj git push no longer pushes new bookmarks by default. Use --allow-new to\nbypass this restriction."],[4710,"jj git push now aborts if you attempt to push a commit without a\ndescription or with the placeholder \"(no name/email configured)\" values for\nauthor/committer."],[4516,"jj git push now accepts --branch