pts a --allow-large-revsets argument that behaves\nsimilarly to jj rebase --allow-large-revsets."],[4684,"jj new now always checks out the new commit (used to be only if the parent\nwas @)."],[4738,"jj new now lets you specify a description with --message/-m."],[356,"jj new v1.0.1"],[4092,"jj new's --insert-before and --insert-after options can now be used\nsimultaneously."],[4081,"jj new's --insert-before/--insert-after options must now be set for each\ncommit the new commit will be inserted before/after. Previously, those options\nwere global flags and specifying them once would insert the new commit before/\nafter all the specified commits."],[4453,"jj next and jj prev are added, these allow you to traverse the history\nin a linear style. For people coming from Sapling and git-branchles\nsee #2126 for\nfurther pending improvements."],[4292,"jj next and jj prev now prompt in the event of the next/previous commit\nbeing ambiguous, instead of failing outright."],[4233,"jj next/prev now infer --edit when you're already editing a non-head\ncommit (a commit with children)."],[4400,"jj now bundles a TUI tool to use as the default diff and merge editors. (The\nprevious default was meld.)"],[3962,"jj now links libgit2 statically by default. To use dynamic linking, you\nneed to set the environment variable LIBGIT2_NO_VENDOR=1 while compiling.\n(#4163)"],[3970,"jj obslog -p no longer shows diffs at non-partial squash operations.\nPreviously, it showed the same diffs as the second predecessor."],[4514,"jj obslog and jj log now show abandoned commits as hidden."],[3895,"jj obslog is now called jj evolution-log/jj evolog. jj obslog remains\nas an alias."],[4716,"jj obslog now accepts -p/--patch option, which will show the diff\ncompared to the previous version of the change."],[3302,"jj op abandon now discards previous versions of a change (or predecessors)\nif they become unreachable from the operation history. The evolution history\nis truncated accordingly."],[3324,"jj op d