ile in addition to the revision DAG at the commit level)."],[351,"Merge branch A into the current change"],[531,"Merge commits can be rebased correctly (Sapling sometimes fails)."],[447,"Merge commits: Yes. Octopus merges (i.e. with more than 2 parents) are\nalso supported."],[1677,"Merge conflicts"],[528,"Merge conflicts won't prevent you from checking out another commit."],[1964,"Merge settings"],[3314,"Merge tools config can now explicitly forbid using them as diff editors or\ndiff formatters. Built-in tools that do not function well as diff editing\ntools or as diff formatters will now report an error when used as such."],[4574,"merge-tools.<name>.edit-args now requires $left/$right parameters.\nThe default is edit-args = [\"$left\", \"$right\"]."],[1307,"Merge/rebase between submodule A and submodule B gives a sensible result"],[1306,"Merge/rebase between submodule and non-submodule gives a sensible result"],[1304,"Merged/rebased submodules result in merged/rebased working copy content"],[1305,"Merged/rebased working copy content can be committed, possibly by creating\nsensible merged/rebased submodule commits"],[1587,"Merges [local, absent] - [known_remote]"],[1581,"Merges [local, new_remote] - [known_remote]"],[1566,"Merges [local, remote] - [absent] in local branch."],[1530,"Merges diff in local branches and tags if state is tracking."],[2490,"merges(): Merge commits."],[1073,"Merging"],[2982,"Merging divergent operations"],[1096,"Merging: When one side of a merge (or rebase) has renamed a file and the other\nside has modified it, propagate the changes to the other side. (There are many\nother cases to handle too.)"],[1268,"Merging/rebasing with submodules"],[4629,"Michael Forster (@MForster)"],[4115,"Michael Gattozzi (@mgattozzi)"],[3443,"Michael Pratt (@prattmic)"],[4313,"Michael Pratt (prattmic)"],[3772,"Milo Moisson (@mrnossiom)"],[2498,"mine(): Commits where the author's email matches the email of the current\nuser. Equivalent to author_email(exact-i:<u