tures"],[3184,"New features"],[3189,"New features"],[3194,"New features"],[3199,"New features"],[3204,"New features"],[3209,"New features"],[3215,"New features"],[3221,"New features"],[3225,"New features"],[3320,"New first_parent() and first_ancestors() revset functions which are\nsimilar to parents() and ancestors(), but only traverse the first parent\nof each commit (similar to Git's --first-parent option)."],[3686,"New fix.tools.TOOL.enabled config option to enable/disable tools. This is\nuseful for defining disabled tools in user configuration that can be enabled\nin individual repositories with one config setting."],[3800,"New fork_point() revset function can be used to obtain the fork point\nof multiple commits."],[4191,"New function working_copies() for revsets to show the working copy commits\nof all workspaces."],[3683,"New git.push-new-bookmarks config option to push new bookmarks without\n--allow-new."],[3682,"New git.sign-on-push config option to automatically sign commits which are\nbeing pushed to a Git remote."],[3783,"New jj absorb command automatically squashes changes from the current commit into relevant ancestor commits."],[4290,"New jj config path command to print the config file path without launching\nan editor."],[4283,"New jj op abandon command is added to clean up the operation history. Git\nrefs and commit objects can be further compacted by jj util gc."],[2909,"New keywords and functions can be defined as aliases, by using any\ncombination of the predefined keywords/functions and other aliases."],[3809,"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.conflict-marker-style config option to override the\nconflict marker style used for a specific merge tool."],[3685,"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.diff-expected-exit-codes config option to suppress\nwarnings from tools exiting with non-zero exit codes."],[3810,"New merge-tools.<TOOL>.merge-conflict-exit-codes config option to allow a\nmerge tool to exit with a non-zero code to indicate that not all conflicts\nwere resolved."