l tools,\nbut it doesn't support conflicts with more than 2 sides."],[134,"Next, restore the contents of 31a347e0 into the working copy:"],[3936,"next/prev will no longer infer when to go into edit mode when moving from\ncommit to commit. It now either follows the flags --edit|--no-edit or it\ngets the mode from ui.movement.edit."],[3580,"Nick Pupko (@npupko)"],[3444,"Nicole Patricia Mazzuca (@strega-nil)"],[3490,"Nicole Patricia Mazzuca (@strega-nil)"],[3508,"Nicole Patricia Mazzuca (@strega-nil)"],[3296,"Nigthknight (@nigthknight)"],[3346,"Nigthknight (@nigthknight)"],[3297,"Nikhil Marathe (@nikhilm)"],[3491,"Nils Koch (@nilskch)"],[1720,"NixOS"],[4679,"No changes (just trying to get automated GitHub release to work)."],[4637,"No changes, only changed to a released version of the thrift crate dependency."],[4744,"No changes, only trying to get the automated build to work."],[4745,"No changes, only trying to get the automated build to work."],[4215,"No code changes (fixing Rust Cargo.toml stuff)."],[525,"No commands fail because you have changes in the working copy (\"abort: 1\nconflicting file changes: ...\"). No need for sl shelve."],[1773,"No configuration is required with fish >= 4.0.2 which loads dynamic\ncompletions by default."],[1472,"No configuration syntax is planned at this time but if we add any, we should\nprobably reuse the compact line syntaxes as much as possible for consistency."],[497,"No current branch. Git lets you check out a branch, making it the 'current\nbranch', and new commits will automatically update the branch. This is\nnecessary in Git because Git might otherwise lose track of the new commits."],[2770,"No methods are defined."],[2691,"No methods are defined. Can be constructed with false or true literal."],[496,"No need for branch names (but they are supported as\nbookmarks). Git lets you check out a commit without\nattaching a branch to it. It calls this state \"detached HEAD\". This is the\nnormal state in Jujutsu (there's actually no way -- yet, at least -- to have\nan active branch/bookmark). However, Jujutsu keeps track of all visible heads\n(leaves) of the commit graph, so the commits won't get lost or\ngarbage-collected."],[4160,"Noah Mayr (@noahmayr)"],[4207,"Noah Mayr (@noahmayr)"],[1917,"Node style"],[4506,"Nodes in the (text-based) graphical log output now use a ◉ symbol instead\nof the letter o. The ASCII-based graph styles still use o."],[1277,"Non-Git 'submodules' (e.g. native jj submodules, other VCSes)"],[1278,"Non-Git backends (e.g. Google internal backend)"],[1235,"Non-git subrepos"],[1253,"Non-goals"],[1322,"Non-Goals"],[4366,"Non-tracking remote branches aren't listed by default. Use jj branch list\n--all to show all local and remote branches."],[4192,"None."],[2396,"none()- ⇒ {} (empty set)"],[2341,"none(): Matches nothing."],[2471,"none(): No commits. This function is rarely useful; it is provided for\ncompleteness."],[2412,"none():: ⇒ {} (empty set)"],[2441,"none()::D ⇒ {} (empty set)"],[2419,"none().. ⇒ {D,C,B,A,root()}"],[2450,"none()..D ⇒ {D,C,B,A,root()}"],[2404,"none()+ ⇒ {} (empty set)"],[1592,"Noop anyway since [local, absent] - [absent] -> local"],[1618,"Noop since [absent, remote] - [absent] -> remote"],[1870,"Normally, when commits are rewritten, the original version (the \"predecessor\")\nbecomes hidden and the new commit (the \"successor\") is visible. Thus, only one\ncommit with a given change ID is visible at a time."],[1575,"not abandon commits which belongs to those branches (even if the branch is\nremoved at a remote)"],[339,"Not supported"],[377,"Not supported"],[414,"Not supported"],[417,"Not supported"],[383,"Not supported (can be emulated with the \"edit\" action in git rebase -i)"],[386,"Not supported (can be emulated with the \"edit\" action in git rebase -i)"],[1226,"Notable use cases and workflows are noted below."],[1690,"Notably, the above workflow creates a new commit for you. The same can be\nachieved without creating a new commit."],[248,"Note 