 install jj via the MacPorts jujutsu\nport:"],[2339,"You can also specify patterns by using functions."],[2453,"You can also specify revisions by using functions. Some functions take other\nrevsets (expressions) as arguments."],[2010,"You can also use a 6-digit hex code for more control over the exact color used:"],[94,"You can also use jj evolog -r on revisions that were previously the\nworking-copy revisions (or on any other revisions). Use jj evolog -p as an\neasy way to see the evolution of the commit's contents."],[1824,"You can also view the repo the way it looked after some earlier operation. For\nexample, if you want to see jj log output right after the jj rebase\noperation, try jj log --at-op=367400773f87 but use the hash from your own\njj op log."],[2557,"You can append -i after the kind to match case‐insensitively (e.g.\nglob-i:\"fix*jpeg*\")."],[4142,"You can check whether Watchman fsmonitor is enabled or installed with the new\njj debug watchman status command."],[2249,"You can check whether Watchman is enabled and whether it is installed correctly\nusing jj debug watchman status."],[2301,"You can conditionally enable config variables by using --when."],[2023,"You can configure automatic addition of one or more trailers to commit\ndescriptions using the commit_trailers template."],[2248,"You can configure jj to use watchman triggers to automatically create\nsnapshots on filesystem changes by setting\nfsmonitor.watchman.register-snapshot-trigger = true."],[2066,"You can configure the revisions jj log would show when neither -r nor any paths are specified."],[2055,"You can configure the set of immutable commits via\nrevset-aliases.\"immutable_heads()\". The default set of immutable heads is\nbuiltin_immutable_heads(), which in turn is defined as\npresent(trunk()) | tags() | untracked_remote_bookmarks(). For example, to\nalso consider the release@origin bookmark immutable:"],[2238,"You can configure the set of private commits by setting git.private-commits